\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AZ COURT UPHOLDS NEAR-TOTAL ABORTION BAN STATE SUPREME COURT REINSTATES 160-YEAR-OLD LAW\b0\par\par\uc2 889 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, HOBBS, ARIZONA, BURCH, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening. And it's great to be back from our coverage of the solar eclipse. We really appreciate you joining us for our special coverage.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We begin tonight with several developing headlines. These threats of severe storms, tornadoes, flooding across several states. It gets much worse over the next 24 hours, eventually right up into the northeast.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AZ COURT UPHOLDS NEAR-TOTAL ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we do begin tonight with the shockwaves in Arizona after that state's Supreme Court has now upheld an abortion law dating back to 1864, criminalizing all abortions, except those to save the mother's life.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In their decision, the Arizona justices referred repeatedly to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  ruling overturning Roe versus Wade. Their decision on hold for 14 days, pending a lower court review. Arizona Governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , a Democrat, saying the ruling creates more chaos for women and doctors in her state. A doctor who performs an abortion could get up to five years in prison. She says voters will have their say in November. Arizona, of course, is a key battleground in the race for president this November. And the question already, how could this decision now effect the presidential race?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ABC's Rachel Scott leading us off tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE SUPREME COURT REINSTATES 160-YEAR-OLD LAW\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Arizona's highest court upholding a 160-year-old abortion ban, one of the strictest in the country, a law written in 1864, before Arizona was even a state and before women had the right to vote. It outlaws nearly all abortions. The only exception, to protect the life of the mother. Tonight, outrage from Arizona's Democratic governor, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR KATIE HOBBS (DEM) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 And the near total Civil War-era ban that continues to hang over our heads only serves to create more chaos for women and doctors in our state.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Under the law, doctors who perform abortions could face up to five years in prison. Frustration from Arizona lawmaker Eva Burch, who recently had an abortion after her pregnancy failed.\par \par \uc2 STATE SENATOR EVA BURCH (DEM) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 A couple weeks ago, I had an abortion. A safe, legal abortion here in Arizona for a pregnancy that I very much wanted. Somebody took care of me. Somebody gave me a procedure, so that I wouldn't have to experience another miscarriage, the pain, the mess, the discomfort. And now, we're talking about whether or not we should put that doctor in jail.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In today's ruling, the Arizona court referring 22 times to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2 's decision overturning Roe versus Wade. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has boasted of appointing three of the six justices who overturned Roe. Yesterday, he said states should make their own laws when it comes to abortion.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 The states will determine by vote or legislation or perhaps both. And whatever they decide must be the law of the land. In this case, the law of the state.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) President Biden says that means that Trump supports state bans like the one in Arizona, which Biden today called "extreme, dangerous, and cruel."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN CALLS BAN "EXTREME AND DANGEROUS"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Biden and Trump both know that abortion rights has won in all six states where it has been on the ballot in, including in conservative states like Kansas, Kentucky, and Ohio. This November, voters could decide in 14 states, and one of them is Arizona, a key presidential battleground. Tonight, the governor with this message.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR KATIE HOBBS (DEM) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 To the people across Arizona, who are concerned about the future of abortion rights in our state, you can make your concerns known at the ballot box, and I encourage you to do so.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, this is really shaping up to be an issue that could affect the presidential race in November. Rachel Scott back with us tonight covering the race for president. And, of course, not just in Arizona, but how many presidential battlegrounds, these are the key states in the Electoral College that help decide the presidential race, will have voters not only deciding in the race for president, but weighing in on the issue of abortion rights?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, we could see this issue on the ballot in several battleground states, including Pennsylvania, Arizona, and Nevada. We know that voters in Florida will have the final say on this issue, and that does raise real questions if it puts a state like Florida in play for Democrats. We know President Biden's campaign is counting on this issue to drive voters to the polls this November. As for Arizona, the justices putting that ruling on hold for 14 days, as a lower court reviews it. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott leading us off from Washington. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240411ek4900002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP: LET STATES DECIDE ABORTION LAWS HAD PREVIOUSLY HINTED SUPPORT OF NATIONWIDE BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 663 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SOLAR ECLIPSE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, BIDEN, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we do move on now to the other major news this Monday night and to the race for the White House. After \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  repeatedly celebrated the overturns of Roe vs. Wade with help from the justices here appointed to the Supreme Court, what he's now saying about a nationwide abortion ban tonight. The Biden campaign pouncing. Here's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP: LET STATES DECIDE ABORTION LAWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HAD PREVIOUSLY HINTED SUPPORT OF NATIONWIDE BAN\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, after months of hinting he would support a national abortion ban, now \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  declaring the matter should be left up to individual states.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 The states will determine by vote or legislation or perhaps both. And whatever they decide must be the law of the land. In this case, the law of the state.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just last month, Trump said he was leaning toward supporting a national ban at around 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 The number of weeks now, people are agreeing on 15, and I'm thinking in terms of that.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But now, a reversal. Today, Trump made it clear, politics was at the heart of his decision, keenly aware abortion rights has won in all six states where it has appeared on the ballot, including in conservative states like Kansas, Kentucky, and Ohio.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 You must follow your heart on this issue. But remember, you must also win elections.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATES THAT BAN OR RESTRICT ABORTION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, President Biden pointing out 21 states have banned or severely limited access to abortions since Roe was overturned.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM CAMPAIGN AD\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just endorsed every single state ban on reproductive care nationwide.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Biden's campaign seizing on Trump's false new claim that both sides of the abortion debate were happy when the Supreme Court overturned Roe.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I was proudly the person responsible for the ending of something that all legal scholars, both sides, wanted and, in fact, demanded be ended. Roe v. Wade, they wanted it ended.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, Vice President Harris firing back.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 He's proudly responsible that 1 in 3 women of reproductive age now live in a state with an abortion ban? If he were to be put back in a position where he could sign off on a law, he would sign off on national abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Biden campaign reminding Americans Trump often boasted of appointing the justices who overturned Roe, taking away a woman's right to choose. Tonight, warning voters not to be fooled.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Trump says he supports exceptions for rape, incest, and to save the life of the mother. He won't say about health of the mother. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott with us tonight. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There is another breaking headline tonight involving \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Late today, a New York appellate court denying Trump's last-minute attempt to delay his first criminal trial now set to begin one week from today.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The judge issuing a one-line ruling, writing, "Defendant's plication for a stay of trial pending the determination of motion for change of venue is denied." Trump's lawyers wanted a stay while they attempt to move the hush money case out of Manhattan, arguing overwhelming pretrial publicity makes it impossible to find and impartial jury. The prosecution saying, Trump is responsible for generates that publicity.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240410ek4800003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BIDEN & TRUMP SCORE PRIMARY VICTORIES RESULTS SHOW WARNING SIGNS FOR BOTH CANDIDATES\b0\par\par\uc2 732 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WIDESPREAD DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 STORMS, WINDS, TORNADOES, RAIN, DAMAGE, YUODIS\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, FLOODING, WINDS, SNOW\par \par \uc2 EARTHQUAKE, TAIWAN, KILLED, INJURED, BUILDINGS, LANDSLIDES\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, STRIKE, AID, CONVOY, WORKERS, KIRBY\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, TRUMP, PRIMARIES, ABORTION, IMMIGRATION, GARCIA\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Britt, thanks very much. We're gonna get the latest now on the race for the White House. Former President Trump hit the campaign trail in Wisconsin as primary voters went to the polls there. Both Trump and President Biden won. Both campaigns also show signs of problems. Rachel Scott is in Green Bay, Wisconsin, with the battle for the swing state. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN & TRUMP SCORE PRIMARY VICTORIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RESULTS SHOW WARNING SIGNS FOR BOTH CANDIDATES\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, good morning to you. And as much as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to focus on immigration and President Biden wants to focus on abortion rights, these primary results do show clear challenges for both candidates in critical battleground states like here in Wisconsin, where a few thousand votes could make all the difference.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, President Biden and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  scoring decisive victories in a string of primaries, but the results showing clear warning signs for both candidates. The former President returning to the campaign trail repeating his lies about the 2020 election, and escalating his attacks on President Biden, accusing him of unleashing a quote "Blood bath at the border." And once again using disparaging rhetoric to describe some undocumented immigrants, calling them animals.\par \par \uc2 FMR PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Democrats say, please don't call them animals, they're humans. I said, no, they're not humans, they're not humans, they're animals.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Biden campaign firing back, insisting Trump is embracing political violence, calling him a threat to democracy. The former President drilling in on what he's calling migrant crime, pointing to the death of 25-year-old Ruby Garcia, who officials say was killed by an undocumented immigrant who she had a relationship with.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP HITS THE CAMPAIGN TRAIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACCUSES BIDEN OF UNLEASHING "BLOOD BATH" AT THE BORDER\par \par \uc2 FMR PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 They said she had just this most contagious laughter, and when she walked into a room she lit up that room. And I've heard that from so many people I spoke to, some of her family.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the family of the victim telling a local Grand Rapids station, that never happened.\par \par \uc2 MAVI GARCIA (SISTER OF RUBY GARCIA)\par \par \uc2 He did not speak with any of us. So it was kind of shocking seeing that he had said that he had spoken with us.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Data shows undocumented immigrants are actually less likely to commit violent crimes than American citizens. And just months ago the former President pressured congressional Republicans to block a bipartisan border package their own party negotiated.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDIDATES BATTLE FOR KEY STATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP FOCUSES ON IMMIGRATION AS BIDEN PUTS ABORTION FRONT & CENTER\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As Trump focus on immigration, the Biden campaign putting abortion rights front and center, seizing on a Florida ruling that will give voters a chance to protect abortion rights on the November ballot, and releasing this campaign ad.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 In 2016 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ran to overturn Roe V. Wade. Now, in 2024, he's running to pass a national ban on a woman's right to choose.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The campaign saying that now puts Florida in play for the presidential election. But President Biden is facing his own challenges in critical battleground states like Wisconsin. Activists angry over his staunch support for Israel amid its war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , organizing a protest vote to send the White House a message.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) President Biden won Wisconsin by just over 20,000 votes. Well, more than 47,000 people participated in that protest vote yesterday. As for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , even though \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  dropped out of the race weeks ago, she still got 13% of the vote in the Republican primary. It's a sign that Trump still has a lot of work to do when it comes to winning over her supporters. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240424ek4300006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INSIDE THE "VANDERPUMP VILLA" BEHIND THE SCENES OF LISA VANDERPUMP'S NEW SERIES\b0\par\par\uc2 1,156 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , GAG ORDER, BOND\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR FLORIDA A