DALLAS CAR CRASH INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAWYER: RASHEE RICE "WILL TAKE NECESSARY STEPS TO ADDRESS THIS SITUATION RESPONSIBLY"\par \par \uc2 CAMPBELL, CRUISE, AFRICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRUISE SHIP PASSENGERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS SAY CREW REFUSED TO LET THEM BOARD AFTER THEY RETURNED LATE\par \par \uc2 CLIFF, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-STOPPING RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELICOPTER TEAM SAVES HIKER CLINGING TO SIDE OF CALIFORNIA CLIFF\par \par \uc2 TAX FILING, ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE, FOWLER, GOODMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: A.I. FOR YOUR TAXES?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAX PREP COMPANIES ROLLING OUT NEW CHATBOTS TO HELP USERS\par \par \uc2 POWERBALL, SVITKO, LOHSE, JACKPOT, LOTTERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHO WANTS TO BE A BILLIONAIRE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE POWERBALL JACKPOT JUMPS AGAIN AFTER NO BIG WINNER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AS SEEN ON SOCIAL, 8:21\par \par \uc2 STORM, WEATHER, TORNADO, HAIL, WINDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR SPRING STORM ON THE MOVIE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THREATS OF TORNADOES, HAIL, THUNDERSTORMS & WINDS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, RULING, REFERENDUM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR FLORIDA ABORTION RULINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT ALLOWS SIX-WEEK BAN\par \par \uc2 MENTAL HEALTH, CHILDREN, PANDEMIC, STUDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUNG PEOPLE & MENTAL HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FOUND INCREASING ER VISITS DURING PANDEMIC\par \par \uc2 BLUDER, IOWA, HAWKEYES, BASKETBALL, WOMEN, VICTORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IOWA HEADED BACK TO THE FINAL FOUR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COACH LISA BLUDER ON BEATING \uc2 LSU\uc2  IN REMATCH\par \par \uc2 BEYONCE, "THE ROSES", NYE\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, SOCIAL MEDIA, REVIEW, PRODUCTS\par \par \uc2 GAME, COMMUNICATION, SIMONE, ENGAGED\par \par \uc2 "VANDERPUMP VILLA", REALITY, TV, FRANCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE THE "VANDERPUMP VILLA"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEHIND THE SCENES OF LISA VANDERPUMP'S NEW SERIES\par \par \uc2 "JUST FOR THE SUMMER", JIMENEZ, BOOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABBY JIMENEZ TALKS "JUST FOR THE SUMMER"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEST-SELLING AUTHOR ON HER NEW ROMANCE NOVEL\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right, Robin. This book has it all, romance, big questions, unforgettable characters and a last page that will leave you with a huge smile. So, let's see what it is. I love a good reveal. It's "Just for the Summer" by Abby Jimenez. And yay, let's clap for her indeed. And I got to sit down with her to talk about it. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She's the award-winning baker turned bestselling author who's developed the recipe for the ultimate romance novel.\par \par \uc2 ABBY JIMENEZ ("JUST FOR THE SUMMER")\par \par \uc2 My books are very funny, but they also have a lot of depth. So, they're going to make you laugh, and they're going to make you cry. This one is no exception.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now Abby Jimenez is back with her sixth book, "Just for the Summer," a modern-day meet cute that will have readers craving more.\par \par \uc2 ABBY JIMENEZ ("JUST FOR THE SUMMER")\par \par \uc2 Justin and Emma share a curse. Everyone that they date and then break up with goes on to find the love of their life after. So, they meet through this Reddit thread, and they decide if they date each other and then break up that their curses will cancel each other's out, and they'll both go on find their soulmates after. And of course, things don't go the way that they intend.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, you're known for creating characters that are multifaceted, have lots of layers to them. And in this novel, that's no different. Who was your favorite character to write in "Just for the Summer" and why?\par \par \uc2 ABBY JIMENEZ ("JUST FOR THE SUMMER")\par \par \uc2 I think Emma was probably my favorite character. She's so complex. She's got this beautiful empathy about her and\u160\'00\'A0this really interesting life experience that's made her who she is as a person. But she does carry a lot of trauma, and that's one of the underlying themes in this book is trauma and how it affects us in relationships as we get older.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When it comes to those heavier themes, Abby says she doesn't take them lightly.\par \par \uc2 ABBY JIMENEZ ("JUST FOR THE SUMMER")\par \par \uc2 I had mental health advisers. I have psychologists that read the book, made sure that I got Emma's situation correct and that it was depicted with accuracy and sensitivity.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The book is also a love letter to Minnesota. Why did you want to set it there?\par \par \uc2 ABBY JIMENEZ ("JUST FOR THE SUMMER")\par \par \uc2 I live in Minnesota. I love Minnesota. It's beautiful here. I write most of my books here in Minnesota. If that's what's authentic to me, it's going to feel like you are visiting that place because it's very easy to write about the place that I see every day.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When not writing or juggling her three cupcake shops, Abby says she's an avid reader who loves a good romance novel.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For readers who might not gravitate towards romance as a genre, what's your sales pitch for them?\par \par \uc2 ABBY JIMENEZ ("JUST FOR THE SUMMER")\par \par \uc2 Romance, particularly modern romance, is smart. It feels very in the now. And most importantly is it's going to give you a happy ever after at the end. So, no matter what I put you through in these pages, you will be smiling on that last page, when you close that book. And if you don't read romance, just read this one. This is going to be your gateway book, and then you're going to be reading all the romances, and you can thank me.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And "Just for the Summer" is available now. If you're already a fan of Abby's, then you know she has her own Abby-verse, where she brings characters back from her other novels. So, you'll see some familiar faces. But if this is your first time reading one of Abby's bestsellers, don't worry. This one can still be read as a stand-alone, and you can keep reading along with us on our \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , @gmabookclub. Guys, I have some here for you. You're going to love it.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm in.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Who doesn't want a happily ever after? That's true.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up, country star Chris Young is here performing live on "GMA." Come on back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240423ek420000v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "NEARLY NEWLYWED GAME" BEFORE YOU TAKE THE LEAP\b0\par\par\uc2 1,764 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , GAG ORDER, BOND\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR FLORIDA ABORTION RULINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT ALLOWS SIX-WEEK BAN BUT GIVES VOTERS FINAL SAY IN NOVEMBER\par \par \uc2 THREAT, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , ELLIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FBI\uc2  OFFICE SCARE UNDER INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER IN CUSTODY AFTER SMALL SUV RAMS INTO ATLANTA OFFICE GATE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, AIRSTRIKES, SYRIA, AKBARI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDDLE EAST ESCALATION?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN VOWS RETRIBUTION, BLAMES ISRAEL FOR