 \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR FLORIDA ABORTION RULINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT ALLOWS SIX-WEEK BAN\par \par \uc2 MENTAL HEALTH, CHILDREN, PANDEMIC, STUDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUNG PEOPLE & MENTAL HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FOUND INCREASING ER VISITS DURING PANDEMIC\par \par \uc2 BLUDER, IOWA, HAWKEYES, BASKETBALL, WOMEN, VICTORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IOWA HEADED BACK TO THE FINAL FOUR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COACH LISA BLUDER ON BEATING \uc2 LSU\uc2  IN REMATCH\par \par \uc2 BEYONCE, "THE ROSES", NYE\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, SOCIAL MEDIA, REVIEW, PRODUCTS\par \par \uc2 GAME, COMMUNICATION, SIMONE, ENGAGED\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back, everybody. It's time now for our series Before You Take the Leap, looking at the must-have conversations before marriage. And this morning, it's all about how to have authentic communication to strengthen your relationship.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, we have two engaged couples here, and we're going to see how well they know each other, and our matchmaker and dating expert Devyn Simone is here with some helpful relationship tips. Thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 DEVYN SIMONE (DATING EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 Happy to be here.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Devyn, I want to start with you, before we start this game, because all the engaged couples out there, who may be watching the show right now, what is the most important topic that they should be talking about before they tie the knot?\par \par \uc2 DEVYN SIMONE (DATING EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I'd say there's three things to keep in mind. One, customize your relationship. This is you all's, you can make your own traditions, your own rules. You don't have to do what everyone expects of you. Number two, check in. I'm sure by now you've talked about the big things, kids, finances, household chores. But check in because people's perspectives evolve, and their point of view may change. So, check in again. And then three, be prepared to adapt because you're not just falling in love and marrying one person. You need to be prepared to fall in love with that same person but different versions of them throughout time to have a happy relationship.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's very good advice, great advice. All right, so, now let's meet our couples. First up, we have Rashada and Mike. And they met at church, and they've been together for a year and a half. As I understand it, they like to dance, they like to wear matching outfits and have a good time. And then over here, we have Abby and Schuyler. They've been together for nine years. Schuyler proposed in Paris. Well done, my friend. They have a one-year-old golden retriever they share, named Bo.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, well, thank you all for being here. Now, we're going to see how well they know each other with our "GMA" "Nearly Newlywed Game." \uc2 Cue\uc2  the music. All right, are you all ready to play? All right, they're ready to play, and here's how it's going to work. I'm going to ask, we're going to ask you a question, and you're going to reveal your answers on your cards, okay. And since Devyn is our matchmaking expert, she'll chime in with some tips. And you're all paying for a $500 gift card to \uc2 Massage Envy\uc2 . Yeah, all right, here we go. First up, this one for the guys. Don't mess it up. What is your future wife's favorite TV show? Show what you got there.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow, nailed it.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, I'm kind of scared by both of your choices. But Devyn, Devyn, you have a tip because there's couples out there who don't have the same love or interest in shows, but this could be an actual moment of growth for the...\par \par \uc2 DEVYN SIMONE (DATING EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 You're\u160\'00\'A0100 percent correct, Michael. So, we call that being influenced in your relationship. And partners who are open to influence from their partners, like watching their favorite show or trying their favorite food, report overall higher satisfaction rates in their marriage. So, be influencers in your relationship.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Love that. All right, so, now, we're going to talk crushes. Guys, we want you to name, I don't know if this is, I think it's girls, we want you to name your future husband's number one celebrity crush. So, ready?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What are we trying to do here?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know, I was a little nervous about this one, but just go for it. Wow, again, these couples are very in sync. And this is something, like, we were uncomfortable asking it, but you're like, you know what, just it's fine.\par \par \uc2 DEVYN SIMONE (DATING EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, being able to be honest with one another in the relationship is important, and clearly, they were honest.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They are honest, a little too honest for me. Baby, I don't love nobody but you. All right, now, we want to know who is the funnier one in the couple. So, make sure you think carefully about this, okay. All right, let's see what you said. Who's the funnier one?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Who's funnier? All right. Okay, this is the first note of dissention. That's funny.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But sense of humor, it's funny you said that. But a sense of humor in a relationship is really important.\par \par \uc2 DEVYN SIMONE (DATING EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 A sense of humor is, a shared sense of humor is really important. And a recent study found that couples who approach conflict with affection and humor reported better daily stress levels, or, like, cortisol levels, which overall impacted their health. So, basically, you can have better health if you laugh a little bit.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, I like it, I like it. You guys can talk about that later. And this one is for the guys. What's your future wife's favorite song to sing along to in the car? Okay, this is getting very interesting. You guys nailed it and a little dissention over here. That's a tough question.\par \par \uc2 DEVYN SIMONE (DATING EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 Maybe she's given full concerts in the car. It is a bit of a tough question, but just so you know, music is a great opportunity to really connect with one another. Tinder issued a survey and found that 61 percent of respondents said that they either formed a relationship or deep connection with someone they met at a concert or music event. So, continue to use music as a connection tool in your relationship.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Great advice.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, and last one, here's the last one. Ladies, this is for you. What is your man's number one pet peeve? Okay, let's see the answers. Being messy, (inaudible)...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's sort of the same thing, right?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They both involve trash.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, they do. Very close over here. This is funny.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Clean up, man, clean up.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, do you have any thoughts on this?\par \par \uc2 DEVYN SIMONE (DATING EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 I mean, you guys are going to keep having these conversations forever. So, just be prepared.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'll tell you what, Mike and Mike on the same page. You're chewing, making noise, you got to get away from me. I'm with you. This has been fantastic, a lot of fun. Thank you so much for...\par \par \uc2 DEVYN SIMONE (DATING EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 Of course.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) At this moment, I just got word from the control room, we do have a winner. And the winner is Abby and Schuyler, Abby and Schuyler, but because this is our show, we can do it any way we want, so everyone's a winner. And you're all going home with $500 gift cards for beautiful massages from \uc2 Massage Envy\uc2 . Enjoy maybe a couples massage. And thank you for your honesty, and great advice. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A nice massage is something we can all agree on. All right, hey, tomorrow for day three of our series, the topics all couples should talk about before having kids. Very important conversation there. And coming up, inside Lisa Vanderpump's new reality show, with the drama taking place in the South of France. We'll be right back with more "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240423ek420000s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAJOR FLORIDA ABORTION RULINGS COURT ALLOWS SIX-WEEK BAN BUT GIVES VOTERS FINAL SAY IN NOVEMBER\b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , GAG ORDER, BOND\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR FLORIDA ABORTION RULINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT ALLOWS SIX-WEEK BAN BUT GIVES VOTERS FINAL SAY IN NOVEMBER\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now the battle over abortion and the major rulings out of Florida. The State Supreme Court is allowing a six-week ban on the procedure to take effect. But it's also giving voters the final say on abortion rights. Rachel Scott has that story for us. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning. Two major decisions.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Florida state Supreme Court has now cleared the way for one of the strictest abortion bans in the nation to go into effect. It bans abortion at just six weeks into pregnancy. That's before most women even know that they are pregnant. And take a look at the impact of this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That means that virtually every single state in the south has now imposed restrictions. But at the same time, that same State Supreme Court also allowing this issue to be on the ballot in November, allowing Florida voters to decide whether they want to protect access to abortion up until viability, which is considered to be around 24 weeks into pregnancy. We know that could have major political implications as well.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In every single state where abortion rights have appeared on the ballot, the side of abortion rights has won, including in conservative state likes Kentucky, Ohio and Kansas. And that now raises major questions about whether that could help President Biden and Democrats in November, Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rachel, so many questions there. Thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240423ek4200005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POP NEWS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,340 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , GAG ORDER, BOND\par \par \uc2 A