ITKO, LOHSE, JACKPOT, LOTTERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHO WANTS TO BE A BILLIONAIRE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE POWERBALL JACKPOT JUMPS AGAIN AFTER NO BIG WINNER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AS SEEN ON SOCIAL, 8:21\par \par \uc2 STORM, WEATHER, TORNADO, HAIL, WINDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR SPRING STORM ON THE MOVIE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THREATS OF TORNADOES, HAIL, THUNDERSTORMS & WINDS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, RULING, REFERENDUM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR FLORIDA ABORTION RULINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT ALLOWS SIX-WEEK BAN\par \par \uc2 MENTAL HEALTH, CHILDREN, PANDEMIC, STUDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUNG PEOPLE & MENTAL HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FOUND INCREASING ER VISITS DURING PANDEMIC\par \par \uc2 BLUDER, IOWA, HAWKEYES, BASKETBALL, WOMEN, VICTORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IOWA HEADED BACK TO THE FINAL FOUR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COACH LISA BLUDER ON BEATING \uc2 LSU\uc2  IN REMATCH\par \par \uc2 BEYONCE, "THE ROSES", NYE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's get some, you are laughing a little too hard over there. How about a little "Pop News," you guys?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 'COWBOY CARTER' BREAKS STREAMING RECORDS\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You got it. You got it, Robin. You were very close. Good morning, everybody, and we're going to cue the song because this ain't Texas. This is Beyonce country, all too clear since her "act ii: Cowboy Carter" dropped on Friday. The album has already shattered records, becoming \uc2 Spotify\uc2 's most streamed album in a single day. And Amazon Music says this is Beyonce's biggest album debut on their platform, out-streaming all of her others. It also had the most first-day streams for a country album by a female artist. I call it the Bayonce boost. Black country artists like Brittney Spencer, Raina Roberts and Shaboozey, all featured on "Cowboy Carter," are also getting a big streaming following from first-time listeners to their music. That's fantastic.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Last night Beyonce was honored at the I Heart Radio Music Awards with the Innovator Award presented by Stevie Wonder. Beyonce revealing what being an innovator means to her.\par \par \uc2 BEYONCE ("ACT II: COWBOY CARTER")\par \par \uc2 You call me an innovator, and for that, I'm very grateful. Innovation starts with a dream. But then you have to execute that dream, and that road can be very bumpy. Being an innovator is seeing what everybody believes is impossible. Being an innovator often means being criticized, which often will test your mental strength. Being an innovator is leaning on faith, trusting that God will catch you and guide you.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Stevie Wonder, by the way, also featured on the "Cowboy Carter" album. He's playing the harmonica on Beyonce's version of Dolly Parton's classic, "Jolene." And it may have been Dolly, in fact, who wished this version into existence. Two years ago, she said in an interview she wished Beyonce would cover "Jolene" like Whitney did for "I Will Always Love You," another one of her great songs, and it happened, and it's a hit. "Act ii: Cowboy Carter" is streaming everywhere right now, and we will have even more from the I Heart Radio Music Awards, including some backstage interviews, coming up later this morning on "GMA3." Yeah. I'm excited about this album. If you haven't heard the whole thing, it's amazing.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "WAR OF THE ROSES" REIMAGING IN THE WORKS\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And hey, guys, do you remember "War of the Roses" with Michael Douglas...\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Kathleen Turner.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...and Kathleen Turner, yes. Do we have a set? Yes, here it is.\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM "WAR OF THE ROSES"\par \par \uc2 KATHLEEN TURNER ("WAR OF THE ROSES")\par \par \uc2 I want a divorce.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL DOUGLAS ("WAR OF THE ROSES")\par \par \uc2 No, you don't. You can't have one.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, she can.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Watch that movie.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The 1989 comedy about a couple in the throes of a wildly contentious divorce, directed by Danny DeVito, I forgot about that, it was a huge box office hit. And now it's being reimagined by, get this, Oscar nominee Benedict Cumberbatch and Oscar winner Olivia Coleman. They will star in "The Roses," and it will tell the story of a picture-perfect couple who have great chemistry, careers, kids, but underneath the facade of a perfect family is a tinderbox of competition resentment. Searchlight president Matthew Greenfield calling the cast and director being called the dream team, stating, "'The Roses' is a wildly funny, bigger-than-life film." It will be directed by none other than Jay Roach.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, what, you're right. Can I, can get an Pop-pause? I don't want, I don't want America to miss the pony. Can you just give it a side shot? This may be the best pony in America right now, America. I just, okay, go ahead, continue.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILL NYE PREPS FOR THE ECLIPSE\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'll return it promptly after the show. And finally, everybody, \uc2 Bill Nye\uc2  the Science Guy is about to have a moment thanks to the solar eclipse next Monday. Everyone's favorite TV science guy has landed on the cover of "Time Out: New York," wow, showing that science in style can go hand in hand. And inside, he answers questions about the upcoming eclipse, saying, "If you have the chance, do not miss it. It may only be three minutes and 18 seconds, but it will change your life." He goes on to say, "The next one's not for 20 years, who knows where we'll all be then. So, seize the moment." Nye is headed to Texas to view it along the path of totality. He stresses that if you're planning on looking skywards, please wear protective eyewear and fit any cameras, telescopes, binoculars, with those solar filters.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our coverage of the eclipse starts right here on "GMA" next Monday, and then you can follow it live on "Eclipse Across America," beginning at 2:00 pm Eastern on ABC, ABC News live, Nat Geo and all of \uc2 Disney\uc2 's family of networks and social platforms. Big day.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, huge day. And that's how I'll\u160\'00\'A0be watching, on an ABC platform, every one of them, so I can...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Did you coin the Pop-pause?\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I just thought we needed one. I mean...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I also like that you have to do a little rap on the glass.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's attention, attention.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240423ek420000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAJOR FLORIDA ABORTION RULINGS COURT ALLOWS SIX-WEEK BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 568 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , GAG ORDER, BOND\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR FLORIDA ABORTION RULINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT ALLOWS SIX-WEEK BAN BUT GIVES VOTERS FINAL SAY IN NOVEMBER\par \par \uc2 THREAT, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , ELLIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FBI\uc2  OFFICE SCARE UNDER INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRIVER IN CUSTODY AFTER SMALL SUV RAMS INTO ATLANTA OFFICE GATE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, AIRSTRIKES, SYRIA, AKBARI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDDLE EAST ESCALATION?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN VOWS RETRIBUTION, BLAMES ISRAEL FOR DEADLY SYRIA AIRSTRIKE\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 UNITED AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNITED ASKS SOME PILOTS TO TAKE UNPAID LEAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIRLINE CITES DELIVERY DELAYS AMID BOEING SAFETY CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 BIRD FLU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIRD FLU CONCERN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEALTH OFFICIALS REPORT FIRST CASE OF HUMAN GETTING VIRUS FROM A MAMMAL\par \par \uc2 MARCH MADNESS, CLARK, REESE, BUECKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IOWA WINS TITLE GAME REMATCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAITLIN CLARK SCORES 41 AGAINST \uc2 LSU\uc2  TO LEAD HAWKEYES TO FINAL FOUR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, RICE, QUINN, DONOVAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHIEFS STAR COOPERATING IN DALLAS CAR CRASH INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAWYER: RASHEE RICE "WILL TAKE NECESSARY STEPS TO ADDRESS THIS SITUATION RESPONSIBLY"\par \par \uc2 CAMPBELL, CRUISE, AFRICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRUISE SHIP PASSENGERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS SAY CREW REFUSED TO LET THEM BOARD AFTER THEY RETURNED LATE\par \par \uc2 CLIFF, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-STOPPING RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELICOPTER TEAM SAVES HIKER CLINGING TO SIDE OF CALIFORNIA CLIFF\par \par \uc2 TAX FILING, ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE, FOWLER, GOODMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: A.I. FOR YOUR TAXES?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAX PREP COMPANIES ROLLING OUT NEW CHATBOTS TO HELP USERS\par \par \uc2 POWERBALL, SVITKO, LOHSE, JACKPOT, LOTTERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHO WANTS TO BE A BILLIONAIRE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE POWERBALL JACKPOT JUMPS AGAIN AFTER NO BIG WINNER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AS SEEN ON SOCIAL, 8:21\par \par \uc2 STORM, WEATHER, TORNADO, HAIL, WINDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR SPRING STORM ON THE MOVIE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THREATS OF TORNADOES, HAIL, THUNDERSTORMS & WINDS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, RULING, REFERENDUM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR FLORIDA ABORTION RULINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT ALLOWS SIX-WEEK BAN\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now the battle over abortion and the major rulings out of Florida. The state supreme court is allowing a six-week ban on the procedure to take effect, but it's also giving voters the final say on abortion rights. Let's go back to Rachel Scott with this story. Good morning again, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning to you again. The Florida state supreme court has now cleared the way for one of the strictest abortion bans in the nation to go into effect. It bans abortion at just six weeks. That's before most women even know that they are pregnant. And take a look at the impact. That means virtually every state in the South has now imposed restrictions. But at the same time, that same state supreme court also allowing the issue to be on the ballot in November, allowing Florida voters to decide whether they want to protect access to abortion until viability, which is considered to be around 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Of course, we know that could have major political implications, as well. In all six states where abortion rights has appeared on the ballot, the side of abortion rights has won, including in conservative states like Kansas, Kentucky and Ohio. So, this now raises real questions about whether this could help President Biden and Democrats in November, Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you so much for that, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240423ek420000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE POST-ROE GENERATION GEN Z VOTERS MOBILIZE AROUND THE ISSUE OF ABORTION\b0\par\par\uc2 2,732 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 GEN Z, VOTERS, ROE, DUVALL, REECE, MORAVICH, HAWKINS, KOMLA, POLLS, AD, LAW\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks for joining us. Tonight, young voters mobilizing around one issue that could decide the presidency, abortion. As several states close out their primaries, abortion rights are increasingly front and center, especially for Gen Z, who've never voted in a post-Poe presidential election. And with razor-thin margins expected in November, the stakes could not be higher. Here's ABC senior White House correspondent Selina Wang.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN REECE (ANTI-ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 It has always been hard to like, convince people that I'm doing good work and it's worth the controversy.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Morgan Reece is a 22-year-old college senior in Bowling Green, Ohio. Three hundred miles away in central Kentucky, 22-year-old Hadley Duvall is a senior at Midway University. At first glance, both Hadley and Morgan are typical college students. But these young women are fighting on opposite sides of one of the country's most deeply polarizing and personal issues, abortion. But their positions might surprise you, given where they are.\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 We can grow on the, the fundraiser. My favorite thing to say is I'm really just pro-minding your business.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hadley is pro-abortion rights on a Conservative Christian campus...\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 What you need to do with your medical choices is not my business, and it's not the next person's business.\par \par \uc2 ACTIVISTS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Hey hey, ho ho!\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...while Morgan is anti-abortion on a mostly Liberal one.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN REECE (ANTI-ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 This is the greatest human rights atrocity to ever occur, that we are allowing the slaughter of millions of children in the womb.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hadley and Morgan find themselves in a post-Roe and deeply divided America.\par \par \uc2 ACTIVIST (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 When abortion rights are under attack, what do we do?\par \par \uc2 ACTIVISTS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Fight back! Fight back!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 40.8 MILLION GEN Z VOTERS\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In an election year when abortion is a key issue expected to drive young voters like them to the polls, their generation's votes could be critical in this year's election. Generation Z expected to make up over 40 million potential voters, almost 17 percent of the American electorate. And voters who say abortion is the most important issue for them are disproportionately made up of the youngest voters.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There is the capacity for young voters to have a real big impact in terms of who wins in these battleground states. We could see some young voters making the decisions that ultimately put someone in the White House.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) You wouldn't know it if you met Morgan today, but she says she was pro-abortion rights until a social media post changed that.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN REECE (ANTI-ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I used to be pro-choice. And I just thought that was like, the normal stance to have. I came across a graphic photo of an aborted baby that just broke my heart.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since then, the Ohio native has devoted herself to the anti-abortion movement, volunteering at pregnancy resource centers...\par \par \uc2 MORGAN REECE (ANTI-ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 We are out here with the "abortion is not right" fall tour.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...serving as president of her university's anti-abortion group and working with Students for Life, a nonprofit anti-abortion organization, organizing events on her campus where many students disagree with her views.\par \par \uc2 CELECIA MAROVICH (COLLEGE STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 Your religion shouldn't tell me what to do. Everyone can make their own decisions.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How has your activism in the anti-abortion movement impacted your life as a college student?\par \par \uc2 MORGAN REECE (ANTI-ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 One woman that I don't even know actually, she sent me a death threat saying that she was gonna run me over with her car. So, it just like, reinforces in me, like, the mission that I have.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Permission in some ways an uphill battle.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM NOVEMBER 7, 2023\par \par \uc2 ABORTION RIGHTS ACTIVIST (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Abortion access is the law of the land in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We visited Morgan shortly after the majority of voters in Ohio voted to enshrine abortion rights into the state's constitution.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How much of a blow was that to the anti-abortion movement?\par \par \uc2 MORGAN REECE (ANTI-ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 So, it was a letdown for sure. But much like all of our other losses, it's not the end all, be all. I mean, we did impact people through canvassing and tabling.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But Morgan is not alone in this fight. Anti-abortion groups have been laying the groundwork for decades, led by activists like \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , president of Students for Life.\par \par \uc2 KRISTAN HAWKINS\uc2  (PRESIDENT/STUDENTS FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 The bottom line is abortion is a bloody business. It's absolutely abhorrent what we do to these children.\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE STUDENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 A 12-year-old girl gets raped, like, how do you feel about that, like those sort of things?\par \par \uc2 KRISTAN HAWKINS\uc2  (PRESIDENT/STUDENTS FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I'm against abortion in all cases. Abortion is a discriminatory stance against another member of our species. At the end of my talk, I'ma go, "For we are the pro..." You need, you guys need to start chanting it.\par \par \uc2 STUDENTS FOR LIFE ACTIVIST (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Okay.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) "Nightline" has followed Hawkins' quest for an abortion-free America for almost a decade.\par \par \uc2 STUDENTS FOR LIFE ACTIVISTS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 We are the pro-life generation, and we will abolish abortion!\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her group, Students for Life, now an army of thousands of young anti-abortion activists with more than 1,400 chapters on college campuses across the country. Many of them showed up for this year's March for Life.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're at the March for Life rally here in Washington, DC. It is a very cold and snowy day. But that has not stopped thousands of people from coming here. They say there's a lot of the momentum for the anti-abortion movement.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Many young people traveling from all over the nation to remind the country of their political power.\par \par \uc2 MAIMOUNA ETANA KOMLA (ANTI-ABORTION RIGHTS SUPPORTER)\par \par \uc2 I'm definitely gonna vote for people who are pro-life. Because I do not believe that a life should just be aborted because it's simply unwanted.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is this country now where you wanted it to be?\par \par \uc2 KRISTAN HAWKINS\uc2  (PRESIDENT/STUDENTS FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 No. I mean, our vision of an abortion-free America has not been actualized yet.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the Supreme Court voted to overturn Roe versus Wade in 2022, voters have overwhelmingly voted to protect abortion across the country, including in some of the most Conservative states in the nation. Nonpartisan polls have also consistently shown that a majority of Americans, 62 percent of them, say abortion should be legal in all or most cases. That number is even higher for younger Americans. Almost 73 percent of those ages 18 to 29 say abortion should be legal.\par \par \uc2 KRISTAN HAWKINS\uc2  (PRESIDENT/STUDENTS FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Does it ever give you pause that your movement is pushing for something that the majority of Americans say they don't want?\par \par \uc2 KRISTAN HAWKINS\uc2  (PRESIDENT/STUDENTS FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 So, when we're having conversations with young people, we're starting there of, what sort of restrictions on abortion do they want? And why?\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While polls show there's broad support for some gestational limit, the reality is that 93 percent of all abortions occur in the first trimester. ABC News reporting on a post-Roe America repeatedly shows that the new restrictions on abortion have endangered the lives of pregnant women in their second and third trimesters.\par \par \uc2 KRISTAN HAWKINS\uc2  (PRESIDENT/STUDENTS FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 No one in the pro-life movement advocates that if a mother's life is at risk and her, and her child has died within her, is no longer living, there's no beating heart, that she must also perish as well. That doesn't make sense.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The law says one thing. But in reality, it looks like something else. So, is there something wrong right now with the status?\par \par \uc2 KRISTAN HAWKINS\uc2  (PRESIDENT/STUDENTS FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 Why I'd say we have a challenge where we have OB-GYNs in this country who are abortion advocates. They're putting their politics over safety and priority.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 68% OF OB-GYNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 59% IN STATES WITH GESTATIONAL LIMITS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 61% IN STATES WITH ABORTION BANS\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While there's no evidence of that, there is data showing that most OB-GYNs say the overturning of Roe has worsened their ability to manage pregnancy-related emergencies. And a majority of them say they're very or somewhat concerned about their own legal risk when making decisions about patient care and whether or not an abortion is necessary.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It seems that there are challenges in the way the law is being interpreted?\par \par \uc2 KRISTAN HAWKINS\uc2  (PRESIDENT/STUDENTS FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 I would say if a woman's life is at risk, and her child has died, and that doctor is, you know, is, you know, doesn't act for fear of losing his medical license, I, I think we have a problem there.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But it's not just women being impacted by abortion restrictions.\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I was a little girl who got a lot taken from her for a long time. So, nobody can take my voice.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hadley Duvall was sexually abused by her stepfather over the course of a decade. At age 12, she realized she'd missed a few periods.\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 We had just came from my middle school, checked me out of language arts class. I remember like it was yesterday. We went and got a pregnancy test from \uc2 Walgreens\uc2 , and I took it right there in my bathroom and it was positive.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She says her stepfather had made plans for her to get an abortion, but then she ended up having a miscarriage.\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I knew what I would've chosen. I would've definitely chosen to get an abortion. But at that time, I didn't even know what that meant.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She never imagined sharing this story with the entire country. But that all changed when Roe fell, and she was featured in an ad for Governor Andy Beshear.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM POLITICAL AD, SEPTEMBER 2023\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXT OF DIALOGUE\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 To tell a 12-year-old girl she must have the baby of her stepfather, who raped her, is unthinkable. I'm speaking out because women and girls need to have options.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The ad was largely credited for helping the Democrat win reelection in Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why do you think your story resonated so deeply with the people in Kentucky?\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I think that my face gives the all-American girl. You know, you look at my background, I come from a small town, a close-knit community. I have a good family, I come from good people. 'm doing all the things that society says are right.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the fall of Roe, Kentucky has put in place a near-total ban on abortions, which concurrently on only be performed to save the life of the mother or prevent disabling injury with no exceptions for rape or incest. Hadley is on a mission to change that.\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 It took me awhile to find my voice. But now that I have, I intend to keep using it to speak out for other girls and women who need it.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Earlier this year, state Democrats introduced a bill named in her honor, "Hadley's Law."\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 Under this current law, I would have had no choice.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HADLEY'S LAW\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) If passed, it would add exceptions for rape, incest, and pregnancies that are no longer viable and expand the current law to protect the health of the mother, not just her life.\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I feel like it helps to give a little bit of hope. It's not where we want to be, but it's just a small glimmer of hope that we can stick together as women.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As a devout Christian, Hadley says her stance on abortion is not at odds with her faith.\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I want them to remember that their religion also says that only God judges. And that they don't have to be the judge.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Social media has historically been one of the biggest battlegrounds for the youth vote, with organizations like Students for Life and Planned Parenthood vying for young voters' attention. Deja Foxx is a social media influencer and abortion rights activist who called upon followers to organize when Roe fell.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM SOCIAL MEDIA POST\par \par \uc2 DEJA FOXX (SOCIAL REPRODUCTIVE JUSTICE ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 It's the summer of rage, babe. It's time to start baking me in the comments and get out there yourself.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But she now finds herself taking the fight to the streets...\par \par \uc2 DEJA FOXX (SOCIAL REPRODUCTIVE JUSTICE ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 How many petitions did we get signed?\par \par \uc2 SOCIAL MEDIA FOLLOWER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Eleven!\par \par \uc2 DEJA FOXX (SOCIAL REPRODUCTIVE JUSTICE ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 Eleven, whoo! That means hundreds of individual signatures.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...going door to door at her home state of Arizona to get enough signatures for a ballot initiative that would inscribe abortion rights into the state's constitution.\par \par \uc2 DEJA FOXX (SOCIAL REPRODUCTIVE JUSTICE ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 There's a path forward after the fall of Roe. There's work to be done. And that fight is coming home, this fight is now up to us. It's no secret our generation is getting (censored by network) .\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And documenting that fight online.\par \par \uc2 DEJA FOXX (SOCIAL REPRODUCTIVE JUSTICE ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 Every time abortion has been on the ballot, since the overturn of Roe, we've won.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What we do know about young voters, especially Gen Z voters, is that they are particularly engaged when it comes to social justice issues. And so, that could be a galvanizing factor to get these folks to the polls.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How much do you think abortion is going to mobilize and motivate young people to vote?\par \par \uc2 MORGAN REECE (ANTI-ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 It's the number one issue on Gen Z's mind.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What do you want young people to think about as they're choosing who vote for in November?\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 I want them to look at, you know, who they were as a child, and how that's changed to who they are now and all the youth that's coming up next. Anything that's said in this election. It might not be you, but it could be somebody you love. And you have to put that into consideration whenever you're voting.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Selina.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VILLA DRAMA\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And when we come back, it's the beauty of southern France with all the drama of home. Lisa Vanderpump spills the tea on "Vanderpump Villa."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020240405ek4200002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NIGHTLINE\b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 This is "Nightline."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE POST-ROE GENERATION\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the post-Roe generation.\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 To tell a 12-year-old girl she must have the baby of her stepfather, who raped her, is unthinkable.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Political ads like this highlighting the voices of young people on both sides of the abortion debate...\par \par \uc2 MORGAN REECE (ANTI-ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 This is the greatest human rights atrocity to ever occur, that we are allowing the slaughter of millions of children in the womb.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 ...mobilizing in this election year.\par \par \uc2 HADLEY DUVALL (ABORTION RIGHTS ADVOCATE)\par \par \uc2 What you need to do with your medical choices is not my business, and it's not the next person's business.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The impact Gen Z could have in November.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We could see some young voters making the decisions that ultimately put someone in the White House.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VILLA DRAMA\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Plus, villa drama set in the gorgeous countryside of southern France\par \par \uc2 LISA VANDERPUMP (REALITY TV STAR)\par \par \uc2 I don't think anybody's quite ever seen the aesthetics that they're going to see in this show.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It's "Vanderpump Villa."\par \par \uc2 REALITY TV STAR ("VANDERPUMP VILLA")\par \par \uc2 Apologize. Say sorry. Apologize.\par \par \uc2 LISA VANDERPUMP (REALITY TV STAR)\par \par \uc2 I did not work this hard to have these little whippersnappers screw it up.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 A little different than the original fan favorite, "Vanderpump Rules."\par \par \uc2 REALITY TV STAR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Not only living together, but working together, you know, there's no escaping.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The French might call it "je ne sais quoi," or maybe "gene se quoi," but it all translates to drama.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And the club Taylor Swift just joined. It's the stuff of her wildest dreams.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 "Nightline" will be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020240405ek4200001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP: SUBURBAN HOUSEWIVES "LIKE" TRUMP MAKES APPEAL TO WOMEN IN BATTLEGROUND STATE\b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , KIRBY, NETANYAHU, BLINKEN, AIRSTRIKES, WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: W.H.: "OUTRAGED" OVER AID WORKER DEATHS\par \par \uc2 POLICE SHOOTING, GRAZIANO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEEN KILLED IN DEPUTY SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 COMBS, RAIDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FOOTAGE OF "DIDDY" HOME RAID\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, BIDEN, TRUMP, IMMIGRATION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP: SUBURBAN HOUSEWIVES "LIKE" TRUMP\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the race for the White House. Abortion rights front and center, and will it put the state of Florida in play? Tonight, President Biden blasting Florida's new six-week abortion ban, one of the strictest in the country, before many women know they're pregnant. The President calling it outrageous. Former President Trump on the campaign trail today saying suburban housewives like Trump. Rachel Scott in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAKES APPEAL TO WOMEN IN BATTLEGROUND STATE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, President Biden denouncing the Florida State Supreme Court's ruling clearing the way for the state to ban abortion at six weeks, before most women even know they're pregnant, calling it outrageous. The President saying, the law puts the "health and lives of millions of women at risk." But Biden's campaign now seizing on the court's other major decision, allowing Florida voters a chance to protect abortion rights on the November ballot. The campaign saying that now puts Florida in play for the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSED AMENDMENTS PROTECTING ACCESS TO ABORTION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They're keenly aware abortion rights has won in all six states where it has been on the ballot, including in conservative states like Kansas, Kentucky, and Ohio. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  often boasts about appointing three of the justices who voted to overturn Roe versus Wade. But today, he didn't want to talk about the Florida court ruling.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We'll be making a statement next week on abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, in battleground Michigan, Trump making his own appeal to women voters.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 You know, the suburban housewives actually like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . You know why? Because I'm the one who is going to keep them safe. They like to say, well, the suburban housewives, I don't know, I think I do great with the suburban housewives, because they want to remain safe.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump trying to turn the focus to the border, and what he's now calling migrant crime.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Every state is now a border state. Every town is now a border town, because \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has brought the carnage and chaos and killing from all over the world and dumped it straight into our backyards.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But, in fact, data shows undocumented immigrants are actually less likely to commit violent crimes than American citizens. The Biden campaign pointing out that Trump himself pressured congressional Republicans to block the toughest bipartisan border security bill in generations because he wanted to run on the issue in November. President Biden urging Republicans to support the measure.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Look, folks, we have a simple choice. We can fight about fixing the border or we can fix it. I'm ready to fix it. Send me the border bill now.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, back to the issue of abortion rights. We know it will be in the ballot in Florida. Tonight, advocates say they have enough support to put it on the ballot in Arizona as well. We could see the same thing happen in nearly a dozen other states, including battlegrounds like Nevada and Pennsylvania, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, abortion rights could be on the ballot in Arizona as well this November. We can hear you barely over the campaign rally behind you. A sign of the times. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240404ek4200007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FLORIDA'S SIX-WEEK ABORTION BAN VOTERS WILL DECIDE ABORTION ACCESS IN NOVEMBER\b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 THREAT, ELLIS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPRING SNOW STORMS SWEEP EAST\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ELECTION, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA'S SIX-WEEK ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are also following breaking inside out of Florida, involving abortion rights. That state's highest court, in a major ruling late today, allowing Florida's new six-week abortion ban to go into effect. It will be one of the strictest abortion laws in the nation. But the court also signaling that voters will get the final say on this in November. They'll vote on this issue of abortion rights at the same time they're voting in the presidential election. So, let's get right to Rachel Scott tonight. Rachel, Florida voters will decide on abortion rights there. And this, of course, could have implications in the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It certainly could, David. And these were two separate decisions.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FL COURT OKS 6-WEEK ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VOTERS WILL DECIDE ABORTION ACCESS IN NOVEMBER\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Florida State Supreme Court has now cleared the way for one of the strictest abortion bans in the country to go into effect, banning abortion at just six weeks into a women's pregnancy. That is before most women even know that they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And then, in a separate decision, that same court allowing this issue to be put on the ballot in November, allowing voters to decide whether they want to protect access to abortion up until viability, which is considered to be around 24 weeks into a woman's pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Either way, this will have major political implications. We know that abortion rights has won in all six states where it has appeared on the ballot, and even including in conservative states like Kansas, Ohio, and Kentucky. And that raises real questions about whether Florida could now be in play for President Biden, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Both campaigns certainly looking at this tonight. Rachel Scott. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240403ek4100004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DRUGS USED FOR WEIGHT LOSS & PREGNANCY WOMEN USING MEDS TO GET HEALTHY BEFORE CONCEIVING\b0\par\par\uc2 1,304 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HOMENDY, GAUTIER, BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, BUTLER, SCOTT, MOORE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BALTIMORE BRIDGE COLLAPSE INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS ON THE MOMENTS BEFORE CATASTROPHIC CRASH\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING, SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPRING STORM SOAKS THE EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS FROM FLORIDA TO MAINE ON ALERT FOR FLOODING\par \par \uc2 BANKMAN-FRIED, SENTENCING, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAM BANKMAN-FRIED TO BE SENTENCED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-CRYPTO KING FACES DECADES IN PRISON FOR MULTI-BILLION DOLLAR FRAUD\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS, HAMMOND, RACISM, STEWART, HATE CRIME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BASKETBALL HATE CRIME ALLEGATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INVESTIGATION AFTER UTAH WOMEN'S TEAM SAYS THEY WERE CALLED RACIAL SLURS\par \par \uc2 LIEBERMAN, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING JOE LIEBERMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SENATOR & VICE PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE DIES AT 82\par \par \uc2 MARCH MADNESS, CLARK, NCAA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWEET 16 TIPS OFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE MARCH MADNESS STARS TO WATCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 COMBS, HUMAN TRAFFICKING\par \par \uc2 MEGA MILLIONS, LOTTERY, CAREY, SAKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHO IS AMERICA'S NEWEST BILLIONAIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WINNING MEGA MILLIONS TICKET SOLD AT NEW JERSEY SHORE\par \par \uc2 CORCORAN, HOUSING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSING MARKET REALITY CHECK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BARBARA CORCORAN ON BUYING & SELLING NOW\par \par \uc2 BEYONCE, "COWBOY CARTER"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "COWBOY CARTER" COUNTDOWN!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEYONCE SHARES TRACK LIST, TEASES BIG NAME COUNTRY COLLABS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTUAL TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, BALTIMORE, SHIP, CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BALTIMORE BRIDGE COLLAPSE INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DETAILS ON THE MOMENTS BEFORE CATASTROPHIC CRASH\par \par \uc2 SPRING BREAK, TRAVEL, AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD SPRING BREAK TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIRLINES BRACING FOR ONE OF BUSIEST DAYS TO FLY\par \par \uc2 DRINKING, ALCOHOL, WOMEN, HEART DISEASE, LINK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN & ALCOHOL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY LINKS HEART DISEASE & EXCESSIVE DRINKING\par \par \uc2 WEIGHT LOSS, DRUGS, PREGNANCY, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUGS USED FOR WEIGHT LOSS & PREGNANCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN USING MEDS TO GET HEALTHY BEFORE CONCEIVING\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back with our "GMA" cover story on drug used for weight loss and pregnancy with some women turning to medications like Ozempic and Mounjaro to help get healthy before conceiving. Eva Pilgrim is back with those details for us. Good morning, Eva.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. It's not uncommon for a woman to be advised to lose a few pounds before trying to get pregnant. But as we all know, dropping a few pounds is easier said than done. So, now some are turning to weigh loss drugs to make it happen.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since January, Anna Parker has been taking Monjouro, a diabetes drug, often used off-label, for weight loss.\par \par \uc2 ANNA PARKER (GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 I spoke to my gynecologist. She agreed that I could take it and hopefully quickly lose weight.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Parker says her goal is to get healthy before she starts IVF.\par \par \uc2 ANNA PARKER (GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 So, far, I've lost about 12 pounds. I'm really looking forward to making a smooth transition to implanting the baby.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But she says she worries about the effects of these medications while trying to conceive, and doctors are cautious because there is little data.\par \par \uc2 DR. RICHARD PAULSON (UNIVERSITY OF SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA)\par \par \uc2 We do not know exactly what the effect is going to be on the fetus. And so, for that reason there is a general recommendation that women stop taking the medications for at least two to three months prior to the time that they conceive.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Novo Nordisk\uc2 , the maker of weight loss medication Wegovy, suggests stopping the medication at least two months before a planned pregnancy, due to how long the drug stays in your system. But pregnancy doesn't always stick to a timeline. Marcela Romero, from Fort Myers,\u160\'00\'A0Florida, says she struggled with fertility for years and started taking Monjouro in November 2022.\par \par \uc2 MARCELA ROMERO (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 After years of trying to conceive with no avail, we actually got pregnant after starting Monjouro, kind of like two weeks after starting it.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Romero discontinued the medication when she discovered she was pregnant but worried about any possible side effects.\par \par \uc2 MARCELA ROMERO (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 Because there's not enough information.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She welcomed her healthy daughter in September.\par \par \uc2 MARCELA ROMERO (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 She's very happy, very smiley all the time.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Experts are hopeful these medications, when properly used, can help women trying to get pregnant.\par \par \uc2 MARCELA ROMERO (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 Losing weight, however that can be done, can make a significant difference. And here we have medications for the first time that really work. I think it's a very positive development in world of medicine and reproductive medicine in particular.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, here's the thing. We don't know a lot yet about the possible effects these drugs could have on a baby. There are animal studies that found there could be risks, but more research is needed. That is why, guys, it is so important to talk to your doctors about what makes sense for you.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, without a doubt. Robin.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT ARE THE FACTORS AT PLAY HERE?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to talk to our doctor right now, our chief medical correspondent Dr. Jennifer Ashton. This is your wheelhouse. You are board certified both in obesity medicine and, of course, OB/GYM. So, what are the factors here?\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, I think first of all, for perspective and big picture, you know, we're focusing on the women who are overweight or obese pre-pregnancy. I want to be crystal clear, extremes of weight on either end negatively impact our reproductive ability. So, in OB/GYN and reproductive health, we will oftentimes take a woman who is either very overweight or very underweight and say, lose weight, gain weight, it will improve your chances for fertility and for pregnancy and make that pregnancy a healthier pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT DO WE KNOW ABOUT THE RISKS?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we just heard from Eva, and, you know, what are the risk factors here? We just really don't know so much.\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, I think there are a lot of different elements at play. First of all, when you talk about women on these medications, which absolutely can do very positive things for their overall health because of, we know the risks of obesity during pregnancy, they can slow gastric emptying, they can make contraceptives less effective and therefore increase the risk of an unintended pregnancy. As Eva said in the piece, we just don't have data on the use of GLP-1 agonists in a pregnant population. So, we always err on the side of caution, in terms of looking at the risk of birth defects. And then again, any time a woman loses weight, she can spontaneously ovulate and conceive.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, okay, but what about women who have issues with their weight, and, during pregnancy, and they can't take these medications?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT ARE NON-DRUG OPTIONS TO MANAGE WEIGHT DURING PREGNANCY?\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, well, first of all, big picture, 30 percent of women go into pregnancy in this country obese, based on their body mass index, so it does make them a higher risk pregnancy. We do follow them differently in terms of that pregnancy. They have an increased risk for gestational diabetes, so they are screened early and often. Reduced weight gain during pregnancy is absolutely safe and possible, obviously attention to their food and being physically active. And then anti-natal, prenatal, fetal and maternal testing, very important.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I know you'll be talking about a lot on "GMA3." We'll see you then, Jen.\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Sure\uc2  will, you bet.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240418ek3s00063\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WOMEN & ALCOHOL NEW STUDY LINKS HEART DISEASE & EXCESSIVE DRINKING\b0\par\par\uc2 738 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HOMENDY, GAUTIER, BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, BUTLER, SCOTT, MOORE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BALTIMORE BRIDGE COLLAPSE INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS ON THE MOMENTS BEFORE CATASTROPHIC CRASH\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING, SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPRING STORM SOAKS THE EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS FROM FLORIDA TO MAINE ON ALERT FOR FLOODING\par \par \uc2 BANKMAN-FRIED, SENTENCING, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAM BANKMAN-FRIED TO BE SENTENCED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-CRYPTO KING FACES DECADES IN PRISON FOR MULTI-BILLION DOLLAR FRAUD\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS, HAMMOND, RACISM, STEWART, HATE CRIME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BASKETBALL HATE CRIME ALLEGATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INVESTIGATION AFTER UTAH WOMEN'S TEAM SAYS THEY WERE CALLED RACIAL SLURS\par \par \uc2 LIEBERMAN, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING JOE LIEBERMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SENATOR & VICE PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE DIES AT 82\par \par \uc2 MARCH MADNESS, CLARK, NCAA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWEET 16 TIPS OFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE MARCH MADNESS STARS TO WATCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 COMBS, HUMAN TRAFFICKING\par \par \uc2 MEGA MILLIONS, LOTTERY, CAREY, SAKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHO IS AMERICA'S NEWEST BILLIONAIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WINNING MEGA MILLIONS TICKET SOLD AT NEW JERSEY SHORE\par \par \uc2 CORCORAN, HOUSING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSING MARKET REALITY CHECK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BARBARA CORCORAN ON BUYING & SELLING NOW\par \par \uc2 BEYONCE, "COWBOY CARTER"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "COWBOY CARTER" COUNTDOWN!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEYONCE SHARES TRACK LIST, TEASES BIG NAME COUNTRY COLLABS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTUAL TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, BALTIMORE, SHIP, CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BALTIMORE BRIDGE COLLAPSE INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DETAILS ON THE MOMENTS BEFORE CATASTROPHIC CRASH\par \par \uc2 SPRING BREAK, TRAVEL, AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD SPRING BREAK TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIRLINES BRACING FOR ONE OF BUSIEST DAYS TO FLY\par \par \uc2 DRINKING, ALCOHOL, WOMEN, HEART DISEASE, LINK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN & ALCOHOL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY LINKS HEART DISEASE & EXCESSIVE DRINKING\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to a new study, just out this morning, that links heart disease and women who drink an excessive amount of alcohol. And most alarming, this study says it's seeing cardiovascular issues even in younger women. Rhiannon Ally is here now with more on that. Good morning, Rhiannon.\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Rebecca. It is no secret, excessive drinking can lead to health problems at any age. But this new study could be eye-opening for women who might think they're, too young to have heart troubles. The study, out of Kaiser Permanent Northern California, looked at the heavy, the drinking habits of nearly 200,000 women ages 65 and younger. So, here's the break down. Binge drinkers are considered those who have at least four alcohol drinks per day. Heavy drinkers are those who drink eight or more drinks per week. Now, the study found those heavy drinkers had up to a 51-percent higher risk of developing heart disease than those who drank moderate or even low amounts. Binge drinkers had up to a 68-percent higher risk.\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is important to point out, though, the study is very preliminary. It is going to be presented at a medical conference next month, but it has not been published in a medical journal, or it has not been independently analyzed. And for those who would like to continue enjoying their glass of wine or a margarita, US dietary guidelines suggest no more than one drink a day for women, guys. And for the men out there watching, it's no more than two drinks per day.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rhiannon, thank you so much for that info. Coming up in our "GMA Morning Menu," many women are using weight loss drug to improve their health before trying to get pregnant. Dr. Jennifer Ashton has what you need to know.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also ahead, superstar Rebecca Yarros, behind "Fourth Wing" and "Iron Flame," is announcing her next book.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, Tory Johnson is here with "Deals & Steals" that will make you look and feel great, all at least 50 percent off. And Sam, got a fun trio with him. Hey, Sam.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What's not to love about us, Babs, Joey King, Logan Lerman. Hey, by the way, when I asked Logan if he was a Peeps person, what did you say?\par \par \uc2 LOGAN LERMAN ("WE WERE THE LUCKY ONES")\par \par \uc2 Am I a people person? Yes. I had no idea what you were...\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, he was like, "Yes, I'm very much a people, no, Peeps. Babs has all the Easter hacks when we come back in just a minute. Stay with us. "GMA" is still rolling.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240418ek3s00062\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUPREME COURT HEARS ARGUMENTS ON ABORTION PILL JUSTICES SKEPTICAL OF ARGUMENTS TO RESTRICT ACCESS\b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR ANSWERS\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, RESCUE, BUTLER, PRTIZKER\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, ECONOMIC, SHIPPING, CARS, CRUISES\par \par \uc2 BUTTIGIEG, BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, RECOVERY, REBUILD\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ARGUMENTS, JUSTICES, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , GAG ORDER, MERCHAN, STOCKS, BUETTNER, BIBLES\par \par \uc2 MASTERCARD, \uc2 VISA\uc2 , SETTLEMENT, MERCHANTS, FEES\par \par \uc2 JACKPOT, BILLION, WINNER, NEW JERSEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EAST COAST WASHOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MOORE, BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, WORKERS, FAMILIES, REBUILD\par \par \uc2 COMBS, RAID, INVESTIGATION, LAWSUITS, SEIZED\par \par \uc2 NFL, RULES, CHANGES, TACKLES, SAFETY, KICKOFF, SCHEFTER\par \par \uc2 EASTER, CHOCOLATE, COCOA, PRICES, MORIARITY, DWYER\par \par \uc2 SHAKIRA, TIMES SQUARE, SURPRISE, PERFORMANCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN STORM\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, BALTIMORE, COLLAPSE, \uc2 NTSB\uc2 , HOMENDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR BALTIMORE BRIDGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NTSB CHAR ON THE LATEST IN THE INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 ABORTIFACIENT, SUPREME COURT, FDA, HEALTH, ACCESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT HEARS ARGUMENTS ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICES SKEPTICAL OF ARGUMENTS TO RESTRICT ACCESS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael, good morning to you, and this is the first major test of abortion rights since the Supreme Court overturned Roe versus Wade. At the center, access to the abortion pill mifepristone, which is used in more than half of abortions in the United States. Over the last several years, the FDA has expanded access to the drug, allowing it to be prescribed by mail, also allowing it to be used up until 10 weeks into a pregnancy. But a group of doctors who oppose abortion rights insist that the FDA unlawfully loosened those restrictions. They also argued, during these oral arguments, that a doctor who opposes access to this pill could be put in a difficult situation if they suddenly have to provide emergency care.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, a majority of the justices on this bench appear to reject that argument. They do seem poised to reject any further limitations on the abortion pill mifepristone. The bottom line, this is now in the hands of the Supreme Court, with a decision expected in June, Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Thank you so much for that, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And coming up on "GMA," our "Morning Menu," Bruce Springsteen back on tour after his health scare, why he was afraid he would never be able to sing again.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Great to see him back. Also ahead, could weight loss drugs be used to help prevent potentially unhealthy weight gain and some other health issues? Dr. Ashton is here to break it down.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, Becky Worley puts carry-on suitcases to the test on the track. And Lara is with two special guests. Hey, Lara.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hi, I am, like, living my best life. Kathryn Ireland and Martyn Lawrence Bullard are decorators to the stars, and they with us for you, with easy upgrades that will spring up your home, your look and for a lot less than a million bucks. The Million Dollar Decorators are here on "GMA." Get ready to dish.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240418ek3r0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GOOD MORNING AMERICAN\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR ANSWERS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning America. The urgent investigation into the catastrophic bridge collapse. Search for answers. What happened in the final minutes before that cargo ship, the size of the Chrysler building, slammed into the Key Bridge? This morning, authorities hailing the dispatchers and officers as heroes. Plus the national economic impact as Baltimore looks to rebuild.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR WES MOORE (DEM) (MARYLAND)\par \par \uc2 The next months are going to be challenging and difficult.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Governor of Maryland, head of the National Transportation Board, and Secretary Pete Buttigieg, all join us this morning. We are live on the scene.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Abortion rights back in the hands of the Supreme Court. Hundreds demonstrate outside the court as it considers whether to roll back access to the abortion pill Mifepristone. What the Justices said, and when they will decide.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "SWIPE FEES" SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 $30 billion deal. The settlement over swipe fees with Visa and \uc2 MasterCard\uc2 , and what it means for your next shopping trip.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Sean Diddy Combs responding to the raid on his homes, as we learn new details about what federal agents seized and the investigation into alleged sex trafficking.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLAG ON THE PLAY?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Flag on the play? Reaction to the NFL rolling out new rules, trying to tackle safety, and what former players like J.J. Watt are saying about it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EASTER BASKET ALERT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Easter basket alert. Chocolate prices flying, with four days until the holiday, how you can still find sweet savings.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICA'S NEWEST BILLIONAIRE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Were you meant to win the lottery? Where the billion dollar Mega Millions ticket was finally sold.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIPS DON'T LIE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And these fans in Times Square hit the jackpot over night. Shakira with a surprise concert. We're not lying.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "Good Morning America."\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240418ek3r00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUPREME COURT HEARS ARGUMENTS ON ABORTION PILL JUSTICES APPEAR SKEPTICAL OF ARGUMENTS TO RESTRICT ACCESS\b0\par\par\uc2 584 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR ANSWERS\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, RESCUE, BUTLER, PRTIZKER\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, ECONOMIC, SHIPPING, CARS, CRUISES\par \par \uc2 BUTTIGIEG, BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, RECOVERY, REBUILD\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, ARGUMENTS, JUSTICES, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the Supreme Court and the high stakes battle over the abortion pill Mifepristone. At the center of this case, questions about restricting access to the drug. Rachel Scott is at the court. Good morning to you, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT HEARS ARGUMENTS ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICES APPEAR SKEPTICAL OF ARGUMENTS TO RESTRICT ACCESS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Eva, good morning to you. And this is the first major test of abortion rights since the Supreme Court overturned Roe versus Wade. And even some of the conservative justices who supported that decision, seemed very skeptical of trying to further restrict access to the abortion pill.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Abortion pills save lives. Abortion pills save lives.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hundreds of protesters demonstrating in front of the Supreme Court. As the Justices consider whether to roll back access to the abortion pill Mifepristone, used in more than half of abortions in the US.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH PRELOGAR (US SOLICITOR GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 Some women could be forced to undergo more invasive surgical abortions. Others might not be able to access the drug at all.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A group of doctors against abortion rights argued that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's decision to expand access to the drug is unlawful, and says it could force doctors opposed to abortion to provide emergency care for women suffering from complications from the pill.\par \par \uc2 ERIN HALEY (ATTORNEY)\par \par \uc2 These are life threatening situations in which the choice for a doctor is either to scrub out and try to find someone else or to treat the woman.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Most of the Justices seem deeply skeptical of the effort to further restrict the drug.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE NEIL GORDON (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Seems like a prime example of turning what could be a small lawsuit into a nationwide legislative assembly on an \uc2 FDA\uc2  rule or any other federal government action.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE ELENA KAGAN (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Is it the only time any court has restricted access to an \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved drug by second guessing \uc2 FDA\uc2 's expert judgment about the conditions required to assure that drug's safe?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The only two Justices who seemed inclined to side with the anti-abortion doctors, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE SAMUEL ALITO (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Is there anybody who can sue and get a judicial ruling on whether what \uc2 FDA\uc2  did was lawful? And maybe what they did was perfectly lawful, but shouldn't somebody be able to challenge that in court?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Melissa Grant's network of clinics provides the pill to women in 17 states. She says the stakes are high.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GRANT (COO CAREFEM)\par \par \uc2 We know that better than 50% of the people who choose to have an abortion right now are choosing to use medication. If we take that away it's going to significantly decrease the access for women in our country.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What's on the line here is access to the abortion pill by mail without multiple doctors' appointments and up until 10 weeks of pregnancy. The Supreme Court expected to issue their final decision in June. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240418ek3r00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUPREME COURT TO HEAR ARGUMENTS ON ABORTION PILL WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION COULD MEAN FOR ABORTION ACCESS\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, DALI, WALLACE\par \par \uc2 SCOTT, BRIDGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR BALTIMORE BRIDGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH & RESCUE EFFORT UNDERWAY AFTER CARGO SHIP COLLISION\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR BALTIMORE BRIDGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH & RESCUE EFFORT UNDERWAY AFTER CARGO SHIP COLLISION\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR BALTIMORE BRIDGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH & RESCUE EFFORT UNDERWAY AFTER CARGO SHIP COLLISION\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR SPRING STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLIZZARD CONDITIONS IN THE MIDWEST, SEVERE WEATHER IN THE SOUTH\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP HUSH MONEY TRIAL SET FOR APRIL 15\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE REJECTS DEFENSE'S ARGUMENTS FOR FURTHER DELAY\par \par \uc2 MIFEPRISTONE, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TO HEAR ARGUMENTS ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT THE COURT'S DECISION COULD MEAN FOR ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To the Supreme Court now and the battle over the abortion pill mifepristone. The court is set to hear arguments in a case about restricting access to the drug, which has been used for decades. Rachel Scott is at the court for us this morning. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Linsey, good morning to you. Those oral arguments set to play out in a matter of hour.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At the center of this case, access to the abortion pill mifepristone. This is used in more than half of abortions in the United States. It has been on the market for decades. But more recently, the FDA relaxed some of the restrictions, allowing the pill to be used until ten weeks of pregnancy instead of seven, also allowing it to be prescribed by mail. A number of medical associations who are against abortion rights say that the FDA cut corners, unlawfully relaxing those restrictions. The bottom line here, whatever the Supreme Court decides will not ban the abortion pill outright, but it could severely restrict access to it, even in states where abortion is legal. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR BALTIMORE BRIDGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH & RESCUE EFFORT UNDERWAY AFTER CARGO SHIP COLLISION\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up, we have the latest developments on the bridge collapse.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAPPER SEAN "DIDDY" COMBS' HOMES RAIDED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSES CONNECTED TO RAP MOGUL RAIDED BY FEDERAL AGENTS IN LA & MIAMI\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Of course. Plus, the federal raid on homes owned by \uc2 Sean "Diddy" Combs\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON EXPANDING SAME-DAY PRESCRIPTION DRUG DELIVERIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW YORK & LOS ANGELES THE LATEST CITIES TO GET THE SERVICE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And the big announcement from Amazon only on "Good Morning America" this morning.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240418ek3q00030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GOOD MORNING AMERICA\b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. The crisis right now after a major US bridge came crashing down.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR BALTIMORE BRIDGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Breaking news overnight, state of emergency. A cargo ship crashing into the Francis Scott Key Bridge in Maryland, causing a dire mass casualty event.\par \par \uc2 DISPATCHER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Be advised the entire bridge, the entire Key Bridge is in the harbor.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 What happened on this massive cargo ship and the final moments before the collision. This morning, the urgent rescue missions underway. Emergency crews deployed divers into the water. Our team is live in Baltimore on the scene.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DEVELOPMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Trump on trial. The date set for the first American president to face criminal charges. What he's saying about testifying in the hush money case.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT ABORTION PILL CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES HEARING\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 High-stakes hearing. The Supreme Court set to hear its first abortion case since overturning Roe v. Wade. How they could limit access to the abortion pill nationwide, even in states that allow it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEAN "DIDDY" COMBS' HOUSES RAIDED\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Federal agents raid the homes of \uc2 Sean "Diddy" Combs\uc2 , searching his houses in LA and Miami. What we know about the investigation after he was the subject of multiple civil lawsuits in recent months.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA BANNING ACCOUNTS FOR KIDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOCIAL MEDIA SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Social media showdown. Florida passing one of the country's most restrictive bans, barring accounts for kids under 14. How social media companies are responding.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "SADDENED AND SHOCKED"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OHTANI BREAKS HIS SILENCE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Superstar Shohei Ohtani speaking for the first time about the illegal gambling allegations against his former interpreter.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONLY ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON'S BIG PRESCRIPTION CHANGE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Only on "GMA." The big change coming to the way you get your prescription medicine from Amazon.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN'S SWEET 16 SET\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MARCHING ON!\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Marching on.\par \par \uc2 SPORTS COMMENTATOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Gets her name in the record books one more time.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Her name is Caitlin Clark, setting another record and narrowly escaping West Virginia. \uc2 UConn\uc2  taking a page out of this winning playbook. They call her Paige Buckets for a reason. And these superstar freshmen leading the charge, Notre Dame's Hannah Hildago, and can anyone stop Juju Watkins.\par \par \uc2 SPORTS COMMENTATOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 There's your buzzer.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 See you all in the sweet 16.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TUESDAY, MAR 26\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "Good Morning America."\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240418ek3q0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BATTLE OVER ABORTION PILL ACCESS SUPREME COURT HEARS ARGUMENTS OVER MIFEPRISTONE\b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, BIDEN, RESCUE, MOORE\par \par \uc2 BRIDGE, COLLAPSE, BUTTIGIEG, DALI, SCHAFER\par \par \uc2 MOORE, BRIDGE, COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 JACKSON, GORSUCH, HAWLEY, PRELOGAR, MIFEPRISTONE, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we do move on now to the other major news this Tuesday night, the Supreme Court facing the biggest test yet on the issue of abortion since the court overturned Roe two years ago. The court now deciding whether to restrict the abortion pill in this country, and what the justices signaled already today. Rachel Scott at the Supreme Court tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OVER ABORTION PILL ACCESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT HEARS ARGUMENTS OVER MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, hundreds of protesters descending on the Supreme Court as the justices hear arguments in the most consequential abortion case since Roe vs. Wade was overturned. The court considering whether to roll back access to the abortion pill mifepristone, used in more than half of abortions in the US. A group of doctors opposed to abortion rights arguing that if a woman taking a pill needs emergency care, it would put a doctor who opposes abortion in a terrible position.\par \par \uc2 ERIN HAWLEY (ATTORNEY)\par \par \uc2 These are life-threatening situations in which the choice for a doctor is either to scrub out and try to find someone else, or to treat the woman.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the Justice Department argued the doctors who brought the lawsuit have no grounds to sue.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH B PRELOGAR (US SOLICITOR GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  is not requiring them to do or refrain from doing anything. They aren't required to treat women who take mifepristone. \uc2 FDA\uc2  is not directing the women who take the drug to go seek out care from these specific doctors.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And today, a majority of justices seemed deeply skeptical of the effort to further restrict the drug.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE KETANJI BROWN (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 I'm worried that there is a significant mismatch in this case between the claimed injury and the remedy that's being sought. What they're asking for here is that, in order to prevent them from possibly ever having to do these kinds of procedures, everyone else should be prevented from getting access to this medication.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Even conservative justices like \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , nominated by Donald Trump, also sounding uneasy with limiting access to the pill.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE NEIL GORSUCH (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 In this case, seems like a prime example of turning what could be a small lawsuit into a nationwide legislative assembly on an \uc2 FDA\uc2  rule or any other federal government action.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The only two justices who seemed inclined to side with the anti-abortion doctors and further restrict access to mifepristone, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What's on the line here, access to the abortion pill by mail without multiple trips to the doctor and up until ten weeks of pregnancy. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  calls this safe and effective. The Supreme Court expected to make a decision in June. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott at the Supreme Court tonight. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240328ek3q00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the horrific bridge collapse here in Baltimore. The search for victims, the investigation tonight. How could this happen?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CARGO SHIP CAUSES BRIDGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The stunning new images showing the moment a massive container ship crash into the Francis Scott Key Bridge here in Baltimore, plunging the bridge into the river. Authorities on the radios just moments before, sending out washings to keep drivers off the bridge. And then the collapse.\par \par \uc2 DISPATCHER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The whole bridge just collapsed.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The ship going dark just moments before impact. The crew issuing a mayday. An eight-person road crew still on the bridge when it went down. Two people rescued, six still unaccounted for. And tonight, what behave just learned here about the ship. Just moments ago, my interview with Maryland Governor \uc2 Wes Moore\uc2 . What happened in the moments before that collision? And our team here in Baltimore with the history of this ship, the crash just a couple of years back.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OVER ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, tonight, the high-stakes battle over the abortion pill, following the overturning of Roe vs. Wade by the Supreme Court. The court now deciding whether to restrict the abortion pill across this country. What the justices said today. What they signaled already. Rachel Scott at the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEAN "DIDDY" COMBS INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the federal raids at the homes of \uc2 Sean "Diddy" Combs\uc2  in Los Angeles and Miami. And sources tonight now telling ABC news this is a sex trafficking investigation involving Combs. Tonight, what federal authorities seized in those homes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP SELLING BIBLES FOR $59.99\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, Donald Trump facing mounting legal bills and that bond now due in nine days. Tonight, Donald Trump revealing he is now selling bibles, charging $59.99.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY SUBWAY ATTACK\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 In New York City tonight, the subway rider accused of intentionally shoving a subway rider in front of the train onto the tracks. Tonight, news coming in of the arrest.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRACKING SEVERE STORMS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We're tracking severe storms across several states tonight. Lightning and damaging winds. Heavy rain also moving up the East Coast, Florida, right up through Washington, DC, Philadelphia to New York City. And we'll time it out. And the heroes here in Baltimore who put out the emergency call just moments before the bridge came down here to keep drivers off the bridge. They saved countless lives.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News, this is ABC "World News Tonight with David Muir" reporting tonight from Baltimore Harbor, Maryland.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240328ek3q00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 US WEIGHS "CONSEQUENCES" FOR ISRAEL VP HARRIS: IT WOULD BE A MISTAKE TO MOVE INTO RAFAH\b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 MOURNING, ATTACK, PUTIN, ISIS-K, VICTIMS, SUSPECTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DAY OF MOURNING AFTER TERROR ATTACK\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, RAIN, MISSING, BROOKER, SHIRLEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR CROSS COUNTRY STORM\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BOND, DEADLINE, ASSETS, JAMES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP'S BOND DEADLINE TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, GAZA, RAID, HOSPITAL, CIVILIANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTENSE FIGHTING IN GAZA'S LARGEST HOSPITAL\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, ISRAEL, RAFAH, CONSEQUENCES, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US WEIGHS "CONSEQUENCES" FOR ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The White House clear in its opposition. Matt, thank you. Ahead of the high level meeting in Washington that Matt just mentioned, Vice President Harris issuing the strongest warning yet to Israel. Harris said the US has not ruled out consequences for Israel if troops do in fact go into Rafah. ABC's senior congressional correspondent Rachel Scott tonight with more of her exclusive interview.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US WEIGHS "CONSEQUENCES" FOR ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP HARRIS: IT WOULD BE A MISTAKE TO MOVE INTO RAFAH\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With Israel ready to launch an offensive into Rafah, with or without US support, tonight, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  not ruling out consequences if they move forward.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Let me tell you something, I have studied the maps, there's nowhere for those folks to go. And we're looking at about 1.5 million people in Rafah who are there because they were told to go there, most of them. And so we've been very clear that it would be a mistake to move into Rafah with any type of military operation.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A mistake, but would there be consequences if he does move forward?\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Well, we're going to take it one step at a time, but we've been very clear in terms of our perspective of whether or not that should happen.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Are you ruling out that there would be consequences from the United States.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I am ruling out nothing.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Those comments come amid a widening rift between Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  and President Biden. Israel insists Rafah is the last major stronghold of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , but Biden facing political pressure, warning an invasion of Rafah would be a mistake.\par \par \uc2 REP ALEXANDRIA OCASIO CORTEZ (DEM) (NEW YORK)\par \par \uc2 What we are seeing here I think with a forced famine, is beyond our ability to deny or explain away. There is no targeting of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in precipitating a mass famine of a million people, half of whom are children.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  called for new elections in Israel, Republicans on Capitol Hill speaking with Netanyahu virtually behind closed doors. In an interview with our \uc2 Jonathan Karl\uc2 , Senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  reaffirming his support.\par \par \uc2 SEN MARCO RUBIO (REP) (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 You cannot have a country in which this threat continues to exist. They have to finish this job. And this fighting can end tomorrow. You want a cease-fire in Gaza, it's very simple, \uc2 Hamas\uc2  just surrender.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott joins us from Washington. And, Rachel, I know that you also spoke with the Vice President about reproductive rights. As the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  hears oral arguments this week in a case that could impact access to the abortion pill. What did she have to say about that?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, and the Supreme Court is expected to take up that case on Tuesday. At the center of it, a debate over whether the FDA should have approved access to the abortion pill, Mifepristone, which is used in more than half of abortions in the United States. In our interview, the Vice President stressing the importance of abortion care remaining widely available, Linsey.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020240326ek3o00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 REP \uc2 MARJORIE TAYLOR GREENE\uc2 'S SURPRISE MOTION MOVES TO OUST SPEAKER MIKE JOHNSON IN RIGHT'S GROWING REVOLT\b0\par\par\uc2 1,059 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 100 PEOPLE KILLED AT CONCERT HALL: MOSCOW MASSACRE\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, RUSSIA, CONCERT, MASSACRE, TERROR, ISIS\par \par \uc2 PRINCESS, CANCER, ROYAL, DIAGNOSIS, NEXT\par \par \uc2 MURPHY, KING, PRINCESS, CANCER, ANNOUNCEMENT\par \par \uc2 RAIN, SNOW, FLOOD, WEEKEND, EAST\par \par \uc2 PARKS, BIDEN, SPENDING, FEDERAL, SENATE, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 NETANYAHU, RAFAH, INVADE, BLINKEN, ISOLATE, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 FAA\uc2 , UNITED, SAFETY, EVALUATE, AGENTS\par \par \uc2 MEASLES, 67 CASES, OUTBREAKS, CHICAGO, INDIANA\par \par \uc2 MARCH, BASKETBALL, BRACKETS, BUSTED\par \par \uc2 HARPER, PARKS, GREENE, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Dang. We start this half hour with a closer look at the top political headlines this week. Joining us are Deputy Political Director, Averi Harper and ABC News White House Correspondent, Maryalice Parks. Ladies, it is so great to have you here, as always. All right, Averi, let's start with you. The dissent within the GOP, Representative \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  of Georgia filed a motion to vacate the Speaker's chair, threatening to oust Speaker Mike Johnson just like we did, you know, months ago with Kevin McCarthy. How serious of a challenge is this to his power?\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is a challenge. Right now, it's unclear if Congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  has the support within the Republican conference to oust Speaker Johnson. It's also unclear what Democrats would do if this comes up to a vote, so, yes, it's a real challenge to his leadership. And he is going to try and avoid the same fate of his predecessor, Kevin McCarthy who was ousted in similar circumstances when he worked across the aisle to pass a government funding bill. Whatever happens this this case, it's going to take a bit of time because the House just went on a two-week recess.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECRETARY OF STATE BLINKEN MEETS PRIME MINISTER NETANYAHU. ISRAELI OFFICIALS TO VISIT WASHINGTON AHEAD OF PLANNED RAFAH OFFENSIVE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Maryalice, another big story this week, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  in the Middle East. We know that officials from Israel are going to come to the United States, come to Washington next week. Still major differences on the way forward, and Netanyahu insists that he is going into Rafah with or without US support.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, this has becoming a really big deal. I mean, for weeks the White House, at every single level, publicly from the podium, in person there in Israel, the Secretary of State, and behind closed doors with the President making phone calls to Israel. At every single level, they have pleaded, essentially, with Israel to not go forward with a ground invasion into Rafah. They have said it would be a mistake, a disaster. I mean, we are talking about over a million people that have taken refuge there in this southern city of Gaza. They had flee other parts of Gaza and they are there, and the US is worried that there is absolutely no way to do a major ground operation and keep people safe.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, so we pressed the White House, I pressed the White House National Security Spokesperson, John Kirby on this yesterday and asked plainly, I mean, has the President lost his sway? It doesn't seem like they've been able to convince Israel to change course. Now, Kirby talked, again, about the fact that Israel is sending this delegation on Monday, so obviously huge stakes for those meetings next week. This is sort of a last-ditch effort for the Israel to try, for the United States to try to get Israel to do something different because if they don't, it raises real questions about what happens next. I mean, how does the US continue to defend sending aid if Israel is doing something the US is so clearly asking them not to do?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN'S CAMPAIGN STOPS IN WESTERN STATES. APPEALING TO LATINO VOTERS IN NEVADA, ARIZONA, AND TEXAS\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, Averi, the President was out on the campaign trail. He was out west in states, including Nevada, Texas, Arizona. What is the significance of President Biden campaigning in those states?\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, this was a part of some of the travel that we've seen the President doing since the State of the Union address to battleground states. On this trip, in particular, there was an emphasis on outreach to Latino voters. President Biden has said that Latino voters are a really big part, an essential part of his re-election path, and we know that Republicans have made inroads with the Latino community during midterms. And so, this was a real effort to sort of shore up the support within a key part of the Biden coalition.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TO HEAR ORAL ARGUMENTS ON ABORTION PILL. LOOKING AT FDA APPROVAL OF THE DRUG\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And look, we're hitting all three branches of power this morning because, Maryalice, the Supreme Court...\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...yes, is set to hear oral arguments Tuesday in the battle over access to the abortion pill. How significant is this?\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The stakes are huge. I mean, this is the first big abortion case in front of the Supreme Court since the fall of Roe V Wade, and we are talking about the fact that over half of abortions in America are from the pill. I mean, people use mifepristone across the country and now access to that abortion pill could really be jeopardized. And, remember, if the Court really changes the fda approval of this pill, it would impact women's ability to get this pill even in states where access to the abortion pill is still legal, so it really gets to sort of the magnitude of this case. And a lot of experts talking about the fact that this is really one of the first times the Supreme Court is potentially second-guessing the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's approval of any drug, so really potentially huge lasting implications here.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Definitely something to watch there. Maryalice Parks, Averi Harper, always a pleasure. Thanks to you both this morning.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240416ek3n00035\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BREAST CANCER ADVANCEMENT NEW TREATMENT OPTION USES FREEZING TO SHRINK LARGE TUMORS\b0\par\par\uc2 739 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "SNOW" LONG, SPRING\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, HAIL, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 BORDER, UNREST, MIGRANTS, TROOPS, BARBED WIRE\par \par \uc2 INMATES, CAPTURED, ACCOMPLICE, CUSTODY, HOMICIDES\par \par \uc2 DOJ, APPLE, MERRICK, MONOPOLY, ANTITRUST, COMPETITORS\par \par \uc2 BLINKEN, ISRAEL, GAZA, CEASEFIRE, \uc2 UN\uc2 , HOSTAGE, FAMINE\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, ATTACKS, POWER PLANTS, DAMAGE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BOND, JAMES, ASSETS, DEADLINE\par \par \uc2 BOEING, SCRUTINY, SAFETY, SLOTNICK, CALHOUN, AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 MARCH MADNESS, UPSETS, OAKLAND, DUQUESNE, FRASCHILLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA ALERTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRANSPLANT, KIDNEY, PIG, WILLIAMS, SLAYMAN, KAWAI\par \par \uc2 HOTELS, SECURITY, KEYS, GREENBERG, HACKERS\par \par \uc2 SQUATTERS, SHOWDOWN, ANDALORO, SHELTON, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, DEALS, FLIGHTS, DOMESTIC, INTERNATIONAL, CRUISES\par \par \uc2 PIZZA, COMPETITION, VEGAS, SICILIAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WINTER WEATHER ALERTS FOR MILLIONS: "SNOW" LONG, SPRING!\par \par \uc2 WASHOUT, RAIN, SNOW, HAIL, FLOODING, SPRING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8:00\par \par \uc2 APPLE, JUSTICE DEPARTMENT, LAWSUIT, ANTITRUST, MONOPOLY\par \par \uc2 SUTTON, CANCER, FREEZING, TUMORS, ADVANCEMENT, OPTIONS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to new hope for breast cancer patients who are unable to get surgery. Our medical correspondent, Doctor Darien Sutton joins us with the details. This could be a game changer. We all have people in our lives who have suffered from breast cancer. What does it mean?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, a true advancement. So, what this is is cryoablation. This is a method that we use in medicine to freeze or kill abnormal or cancerous cells. So, I want to show you some results of this recent publication and this study. It's done at \uc2 Memorial Sloan Kettering\uc2  and this is a procedure done by interventional radiologists. So, this option is mainly for patients who otherwise don't have the option for surgery for one reason or another, but mainly historically it's only used in smaller breast tumors. The reason why this is significant is because these 60 patients had an average tumor size of about 2.5 centimeters, which it's closer to the average size in which breast cancer is diagnosed and the results is that 90 percent were cancer-free a year later...\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) 90 percent?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...which is absolutely incredible, comparative to just having no option of surgery alone.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's incredible. And when would it be available?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, this is something that is already available now, but it's mainly studied in smaller masses, so we'll have to wait to see more results in terms of the long-term success on larger masses. But, for anyone going through the process of breast cancer treatment, it's important to know that your treatment is individual to you based on your history, your current diagnosis, and your goals of plan, or your plan of your, or your goals of that treatment, so talking to your oncologist is the first step.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Real quickly, is there something you should say to your oncologist if you want them to pursue this?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, this procedure is called cryoablation and it's usually brought up for patients who can't undergo surgery for one reason or another, so that's when you step down that road.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Doctor Darien Sutton, thank you very much for breaking that down.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Of course.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:11 HOUSING MARKET REALITY CHECK\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, coming up in our "gma" Morning Menu, a housing market reality check. Are you better off buying or renting? The new research this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:14 VAPING AS A GATEWAY?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also, the teen who says that vaping was the gateway to other substances, eventually landing her in rehab. She has a message about vaping she wants all teens to hear.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:17 SUPERMARKET SAVINGS HACKS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, the supermarket hacks to help take a bite out of your grocery bill.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:21 THE RIGHT STUFF: TRAVEL ESSENTIALS!\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Lori B is here with travel gear to make getting away easier than ever. She also is going to tell you what to do in flight apparently. It's coming up right here on "GMA." I feel safe already.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA, FRIDAY, MAR 22\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240416ek3m0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:00 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 625 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "SNOW" LONG, SPRING\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, HAIL, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 BORDER, UNREST, MIGRANTS, TROOPS, BARBED WIRE\par \par \uc2 INMATES, CAPTURED, ACCOMPLICE, CUSTODY, HOMICIDES\par \par \uc2 DOJ, APPLE, MERRICK, MONOPOLY, ANTITRUST, COMPETITORS\par \par \uc2 BLINKEN, ISRAEL, GAZA, CEASEFIRE, \uc2 UN\uc2 , HOSTAGE, FAMINE\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, ATTACKS, POWER PLANTS, DAMAGE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BOND, JAMES, ASSETS, DEADLINE\par \par \uc2 BOEING, SCRUTINY, SAFETY, SLOTNICK, CALHOUN, AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 MARCH MADNESS, UPSETS, OAKLAND, DUQUESNE, FRASCHILLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA ALERTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRANSPLANT, KIDNEY, PIG, WILLIAMS, SLAYMAN, KAWAI\par \par \uc2 HOTELS, SECURITY, KEYS, GREENBERG, HACKERS\par \par \uc2 SQUATTERS, SHOWDOWN, ANDALORO, SHELTON, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, DEALS, FLIGHTS, DOMESTIC, INTERNATIONAL, CRUISES\par \par \uc2 PIZZA, COMPETITION, VEGAS, SICILIAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WINTER WEATHER ALERTS FOR MILLIONS: "SNOW" LONG, SPRING!\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8:00 AM. "Snow" long, spring. The winter weather alerts for millions as we head into the weekend. The two major storms on the move right now with heavy snow, hail, and flooding across the country. Ginger has the track and timing.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ SUES APPLE, WHAT IT MEANS FOR IPHONE USERS: TAKING A "BITE" OUT OF APPLE?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Taking a bite out of \uc2 Apple\uc2 ? Should the company be broken up? Why the Justice Department is suing the tech giant, and what it means for everyone who uses an iPhone.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA HEALTH ALERT: NEW BREAST CANCER STUDY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 "Gma" health alert. The new hope for breast cancer patients who are unable to get surgery. Doctor Sutton is here with the new study and what to know about freezing tumors.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT HOME BUYERS AND RENTERS SHOULD KNOW: BUYING VS RENTING, WHICH IS CHEAPER?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 To buy or to rent? That is the question. The new research on what's cheaper, and the best option for you in the long run. What home buyers and renters need to know.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VAPING AS A GATEWAY. VAPE NATION\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Vape nation. The teen who says her vaping was a gateway.\par \par \uc2 ELLE WEIGHTMAN (FORMER VAPER)\par \par \uc2 It led into weed and then it did lead me into smoking cigarettes and then also lsd.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 What she wants other teens to know, the signs of dependency and how parents can navigate the tough conversations.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EASY WAYS TO CUT YOUR GROCERY BILL: SUPERMARKET HACKS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Supermarket hacks. From coupon apps to cash back credit cards. The ways to beat inflation and take a bite out of your grocery bill.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE BEST TRAVEL ESSENTIALS: THE RIGHT STUFF\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And time to get ready for your spring break get away. Lori Bergamotto is here with "The Right Stuff" to make your trip a breeze. And she's saying...\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "gma."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Lori is now a flight attendant.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, Lori.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes, and Brad.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. Yes, and Brad's getting a cocktail at work. There we go. We want to thank you all for being with us on this Friday morning. And with high prices at the grocery store, we're looking at ways to stretch what's in your pantry. Top food blogger, Alyssa Rivers is here with some delicious recipes, including her Friday French toast that her four kids love. You don't want to miss that.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Can't wait to make some Saturday French toast using her Friday recipe. Also ahead, the new study on treating some breast cancer patients without surgery. Doctor Darien Sutton is here with what you need to know.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240416ek3m0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STOLEN CHILDHOOD 7TH GRADER CAUGHT IN THE MIDDLE OVER BLOCKED ABORTION ACCESS\b0\par\par\uc2 2,147 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BALTHROP, CRAWFORD, ABBOTT, SALGANICOFF\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening, and thank you for joining us. I'm Trevor Ault. Tonight, we take you to Mississippi, ground zero in the battle over abortion rights and home to the case that led the Supreme Court to overturn Roe v. Wade. And in this post-Roe world, where doctors who perform abortions are threatened with jail time and losing their licenses, we meet the middle schooler who was raped and had to carry her baby to term, becoming a mother at only 13 years old. Here's ABC's Rachel Scott. And we warn you, you may find this report disturbing.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What do you like to do when you're out of school?\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY (VICTIM OF RAPE AND HAD TO CARRY BABY TO TERM)\par \par \uc2 Get on my phone. Do TikTok.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) TikTok?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ashley is everything you think a typical seventh grader would be. But not everything is as it seems. At just 13 years old, Ashley became a mom to a little baby boy nicknamed Peanut. They've asked us not to show their faces or use their real names.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tell me about what the last year has been like for you?\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY (VICTIM OF RAPE AND HAD TO CARRY BABY TO TERM)\par \par \uc2 Kind of good. But not that good, though.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Perhaps the understatement of the year, if you ask her mother, who found out her daughter was pregnant by rape.\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 When the nurse came in, the police came in. I'm like, what the hell? What is going on?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As a mom, when your listening to your daughter describe at 12 years old that she was raped, did you think that there would be an option for you in this state?\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Yes. A rape should be, like, you automatically you can have an abortion.\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA BALTHROP (OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY)\par \par \uc2 You see this timid little girl. I mean, she's literally a little girl. And she was like a deer in the headlights. She had no idea what was going on.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This young family story now center stage in the raging debate after the overturning of Roe v. Wade. Mississippi has banned abortion, but does allow it in cases of rape. So, by all the rules, Ashley should have qualified for one. But here she is with an 8-month-old baby. Why? As states keep passing new abortion restrictions, rape victims are caught in a web of conflicting laws and confusion. Left asking the question, what do I do? And often finding no answers.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, what did you think when you realized that your baby is going to have to deliver this baby?\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 She was scared and sad. She didn't want to go through it.\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA BALTHROP (OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY)\par \par \uc2 That was probably one of those days that will just stick in my head forever. I'm sorry, I'm getting a little emotional. It's sad. I think about a woman, a girl, with no rights of her own basically. She can't make a decision about her own body.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the fall of Roe, the number of rape-related pregnancies in states with restrictions is in the tens of thousands. It's become a national flashpoint. And in some states with no or minimal exceptions for rape, politicians left defending those laws.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR GREG ABBOTT (REP) (TEXAS)\par \par \uc2 Texas will work tirelessly to make sure that we eliminate all rapists from the streets of Texas.\par \par \uc2 STATE SENATOR SANDY CRAWFORD (REP) (MISSOURI)\par \par \uc2 God is perfect. God does not make mistakes. And for some reason, he allows that to happen.\par \par \uc2 ALINA SALGANICOFF (DIR WOMEN'S HEALTH POLICY KAISER FAMILY FOUNDATION)\par \par \uc2 I think it could be fair to say that there is a lot of confusion and misinformation about abortion across the country.\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We're happy.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Regina never imagined in her wildest dreams that she would be a grandmother at just 33 years old.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's been a really tough last year for you and your family.\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Oh, yes, very tough. Like, I ain't cried as much as I did last year.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you struggle to make ends meet?\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Yes. It's hard. Very hard, especially for people with kids.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Regina has three kids, all girls. She holds down a job during the day and attends nursing school. Life was hard but doable. One of the poorest counties in the poorest state in the country. That was until late 2022 when her middle daughter, who we will call Ashley, started withdrawing. She quit the cheer team and stopped going outside. Then Ashley started getting sick, really sick.\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 She ended up throwing up. She was throwing up a lot. And took her to the hospital, they took her to the back. The nurse is like, "You're pregnant." And that's when I just broke down and started crying. Baby, she's just 12. She don't know nothing about have no babies, nothing.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) There wasn't even enough time for the shock to wear off before the next bomb hit. Ashley said she had been raped by a stranger in her own yard.\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Put his hands over her face, over her mouth, and took her to the side of the house, to the back, and stuck his stuff inside her. Then I was like, that's rape. She didn't know him. She didn't know his name, nothing.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To hear what she's describing at 12 years old...\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I was hurt, baby. My heart broke.\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA BALTHROP (OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY)\par \par \uc2 I was on call at the hospital.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Erika Balthrop is a board-certified OB-GYN, one of only seven the Mississippi delta region.\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA BALTHROP (OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY)\par \par \uc2 I performed the ultrasound, and the two of them watching it together and mom, tears are just streaming down their face.\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Eleven weeks. Eleven weeks. And I asked about options. One of the options, abortion. She said, the closest one is in Chicago. I said, Chicago? That's like $800, $1,500 to have an abortion up there. I had to drive, had to leave work, I can't afford that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MOST RESTRICTIVE ABORTION BANS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the fall of Roe, all the states surrounding Mississippi instituted similar bans and restrictions. Some without rape exceptions at all. Abortion access basically disappeared across the whole region.\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA BALTHROP (OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY)\par \par \uc2 None in Tennessee. None next door in Arkansas. None next door in Alabama. None.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, the only option for a woman that can afford to travel is to travel hundreds of miles away?\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA BALTHROP (OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY)\par \par \uc2 Take off work, find a sitter, do what they have to do.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While Mississippi law does include that exception for rape, those cases must be documented with law enforcement. Ashley's rape was reported to police. But with so much confusion about the laws, Regina didn't know they could use that to ask for help. And even finding a doctor to do an abortion would be a challenge.\par \par \uc2 ALINA SALGANICOFF (DIR WOMEN'S HEALTH POLICY KAISER FAMILY FOUNDATION)\par \par \uc2 She was failed by the system because she had a rape that she actually reported. Physicians have so much at stake in terms of losing their medical license, financial penalties and, in some cases, criminalization leading to jail time.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If you meet the exception and you can afford to still get an abortion in this state, where do you go?\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA BALTHROP (OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY)\par \par \uc2 You can go to any OB office if they are willing.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If they are willing.\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA BALTHROP (OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY)\par \par \uc2 The provider has to be willing. Most people wouldn't do it, here in this state. They would refer you out.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you believe that these laws are designed to make it nearly impossible, even for a victim of rape, to have access to an abortion?\par \par \uc2 DR ERICA BALTHROP (OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY)\par \par \uc2 It's a loaded question. Yeah, I do. I do.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The numbers back that up. In 2021, there were about 3,800 abortions provided in Mississippi. But the \uc2 Mississippi Department of Health\uc2  said that, in all of 2023, there were only four abortion exceptions granted in the entire state. They did not track whether any of those were in cases of rape. We reached out to a number of Mississippi hospitals to ask about protocol in rape exceptions. None wanted to comment specifically. And yet the numbers also show, across the 14 states that restricted abortion, researchers estimated using historical data there may have been nearly 65,000 pregnancies caused by rape.\par \par \uc2 ALINA SALGANICOFF (DIR WOMEN'S HEALTH POLICY KAISER FAMILY FOUNDATION)\par \par \uc2 The reality is that rapes are underreported. And so, when you have a situation where you have an abortion ban that requires a report, women are much less likely to use that pathway to get an abortion when they feel that they need one.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We wanted to ask lawmakers in Mississippi about cases like Ashley's. We repeatedly reached out to the office of Governor Tate Reaves and to several state lawmakers, including some who had talked about eliminating the rape exception. We also reached out to Mississippi senators and representatives in Washington. None responded. Regina decided to keep her daughter's pregnancy private, homeschooling Ashley. Then over the summer of 2023, after turning 13, she gave birth to a son.\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Shouldn't have to do this. It's not her time to go through this. They took my child's innocence.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Police arrested the accused rapist last year. Regina says they've used the baby's DNA to prove the link. He remains behind bars, charged with felony rape.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Was that any sort of relief?\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Yes. It's justice, baby.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Regina says her priority now is making sure her daughter can still be a kid, which means raising her grandson herself.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Did Ashley start to realize what had just happened in this situation?\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Ashley knows she had a baby. I let her be a child. So, I raise him. And there she goes.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When Ashley arrives fresh off the school bus, she jumps in to help. But even just helping is a lot for a kid.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Describe like what your typical day is like. You mentioned you go to school, and then you come home and changing diapers, making bottles?\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY (VICTIM OF RAPE AND HAD TO CARRY BABY TO TERM)\par \par \uc2 I don't like changing Pampers like that.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You stay busy between homework and caring for the baby?\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY (VICTIM OF RAPE AND HAD TO CARRY BABY TO TERM)\par \par \uc2 It can be a lot though. Feed him, take his bath.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You've got a lot to juggle.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY (VICTIM OF RAPE AND HAD TO CARRY BABY TO TERM)\par \par \uc2 Yes, a lot.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Regina and Ashley say they want the world to know the real-world impacts of laws like these on real families like theirs.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Should your daughter, who told you she was raped at 12 years old, have had to give birth?\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 No, ma'am. You shouldn't have to give birth to your rapist's child.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What are your hopes for Ashley?\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 She wants to be a nurse. I'm going to continue raising the baby, let her finish her childhood. I want her to go to college. Be that nurse. Get me up that hill.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHAGGY\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we come back, we shift gears. One-on-one with Shaggy, who says joining the Marines during the Persian Gulf War actually helped shape his reggae sound.\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020240322ek3k00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HANNAH STORM ONE-ON-ONE ESPN ANCHOR SHARES PERSONAL NEWS\b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, ABBOTT, SB4\par \par \uc2 RACISM, SENTENCING, SHABAZZ, WRAY, JENKINS, PARKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER DEPUTIES SENTENCED FOR TORTURE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ELECTION, SCHUMER, EMHOFF, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 NAVARRO, TRUMP, PRISON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-TRUMP AIDE REPORTS TO PRISON\par \par \uc2 HOLLINGWORTH, BIDEN, ISRAEL, WAR, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , NETANYAHU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NETANYAHU VOWS RAFAH OFFENSIVE\par \par \uc2 HAITI, EVACUATIONS, CRISIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. PLANS TO RESCUE MORE AMERICANS\par \par \uc2 PRINCESS KATE, QUEEN ELIZABETH II, PICTURE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AGENCY: QUEEN'S PHOTO ALTERED\par \par \uc2 BANK, ROBBERY, ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE: CHILDREN ROBBED BANK\par \par \uc2 INTERMITTENT FASTING, HEART, POWERBALL, MEGA MILLIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 STORM, BREAST CANCER, DCIS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, tonight here, long-time \uc2 ESPN\uc2  anchor Hannah Storm, you know her from "Sportscenter," sitting down with our Robin Roberts, revealing her breast cancer diagnose know situation and her message with three daughters of her own.\par \par \uc2 HANNAH STORM (ESPN ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 The doctor said, I'm so surprised, but you have ductal carcinoma in situ. You have DCIS, the earliest form of breast cancer. And I was like DCIS? I've never heard of this in my life.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How did you handle that?\par \par \uc2 HANNAH STORM (ESPN ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 I was shocked because, again, I had mammograms every year. I have no risk factors. I have no breast cancer in my family. I did not have a lump. I did not have pain. I don't have any genetic predisposition to breast cancer. I got to say, I was shocked. I was scared.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But how are you today?\par \par \uc2 HANNAH STORM (ESPN ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 I'm good. Really good. Really, really good. I'm very, very, very lucky, because they found it so early. What I had is a lumpectomy. The surgery was successful. I was able to go back to work, cover the Super Bowl. I'm also taking a drug called Tamoxifen.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tamoxifen.\par \par \uc2 HANNAH STORM (ESPN ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 I'm taking this for the next three years.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now you decided to let women know the importance of getting those screenings.\par \par \uc2 HANNAH STORM (ESPN ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 The more that you talk about it, and I think just demystify it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly.\par \par \uc2 HANNAH STORM (ESPN ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 And it's okay to talk about, it's okay to share. You know, whenever you're ready.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's the key. And you have three daughters.\par \par \uc2 HANNAH STORM (ESPN ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 And I have three daughters, and that makes it even more important, right? Because you want to think about your family. There they are.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HANNAH STORM (ESPN ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 But, you know, I think about having daughters and the importance of them understanding advocating for their health, and what you can do. You can find out, and you need to find out. And don't be afraid to have a mammogram. Be afraid not to. Be afraid of what you don't know.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, what you can't find out.\par \par \uc2 HANNAH STORM (ESPN ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. You're the best.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hannah, and it's so wonderful to see you.\par \par \uc2 HANNAH STORM (ESPN ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 You're the best. Make your mess, your message, right? Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you for sharing that. You're doing it. You're doing it.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Always pulling for Hannah. I'll see you tomorrow. Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240322ek3j00033\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW PUSH FOR WOMEN'S HEALTH PRESIDENT BIDEN ISSUING EXECUTIVE ORDER ON WOMEN'S HEALTH RESEARCH\b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPRING FREEZE\par \par \uc2 SPRING BREAK, VIOLENCE, SHOOTING, SUSPECT, HOFFMAN, TATOR\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , RALLY, CONVICTS, JAN 6TH, BLOODBATH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , GAZA, AL-SHIFA, RAID, CIVILIANS\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, ELECTION, PROTESTS, NAVALNY\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, WOMEN, HEALTH, RESEARCH, EXECUTIVE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is true. All right, Tom, thank you. Not to President Biden, he's set to issue a wide ranging executive order to promote research on women's health. Our senior White House correspondent Selina Wang has those details for us. Good morning, Selina.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW PUSH FOR WOMEN'S HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN ISSUING EXECUTIVE ORDER ON WOMEN'S HEALTH RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Robin. The White House is calling this the most comprehensive action ever taken by a president to advance women's health research. Now this officials say the goal here is to make sure that women get the answers that they need about their health, saying for far too long medical research has focused on men and left women out.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now the President, he is directing federal agencies to collect more data on women's health, and this also adds $200 million in youth funding for new research. This includes around menopause and conditions like osteoporosis that are more likely to occur after menopause. All of this, Robin, coming amid an election year.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As the election heats up and the President, he's trying to position himself as a champion of women's health, and blaming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for taking away women's reproductive rights. President Biden, he's also urging Congress to step into close that medical research gap. He's urging Congress to approve $12 billion in new funding for women's health research. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240405ek3i00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INSPIRING WEIGHT LOSS JOURNEY HOW ONE MAN LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,829 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WINTER STORM, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WINTER BLAST SLAMMING WEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW, WIND & AVALANCHE ALERTS FROM CALIFORNIA TO COLORADO\par \par \uc2 BOEING, AMERICAN AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN AIRLINES FLIGHT MAKES EMERGENCY LANDING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LATEST INCIDENT INVOLVING BOEING JET AMID GROWING SCRUTINY\par \par \uc2 PELOSI, GALLAGHER, ROY, CHEW, CRENSHAW, TIKTOK, BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE PASSES BILL TARGETING TIKTOK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOCIAL PLATFORM COULD FACE U.S. BAN UNLESS SOLD BY CHINESE PARENT COMPANY\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , WILLIS, ELECTION INTERFERENCE, RULING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SURPRISE RULING IN GEORGIA ELECTION INTERFERENCE CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE DISMISSES SIX COUNTS AGAINST TRUMP & CO-DEFENDANTS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, HAITI, ALBOM, DOLAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE TO RESCUE AMERICANS STRANDED IN HAITI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MARINES SENT TO PROTECT U.S. EMBASSY AMID GROWING CHAOS\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAMILY DOLLAR & DOLLAR TREE TO CLOSE 1,000 STORES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOWNSIZING RAISES CONCERNS ABOUT FOOD INSECURITY\par \par \uc2 DOGS, STRESS, BURROWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR BRAIN ON PUPPIES!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT A NEW STUDY REVEALS ABOUT DOGS & OUR HAPPINESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 MATTINGLY, SAND HOLE, COLLAPSE, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARENTS BREAK THEIR SILENCE ABOUT BEACH TRAGEDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7-YEAR-OLD KILLED AFTER SAND HOLE CAVED IN ON HER & BROTHER\par \par \uc2 HEUERMANN, ELLERUP, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECTED LONG ISLAND SERIAL KILLER'S ESTRANGED WIFE SPEAKS OUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAYS SHE IS GIVING HIM "THE BENEFIT OF THE DOUBT" IN NEW STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 ELI LILLY\uc2 , AMAZON PHARMACY, MARTIN, SELTZER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRIME TIME FOR WEIGHT LOSS?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON TEAMS UP WITH \uc2 ELI LILLY\uc2  TO DELIVER POPULAR WEIGHT LOSS & DIABETES DRUGS\par \par \uc2 'NSYNC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OLIVIA MUNN'S BREAST CANCER FIGHT, 8:18\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, HAIL, TORNADO, SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR CROSS-COUNTRY STORM ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS IN THE PATH OF TORNADOES, HAIL & SNOW\par \par \uc2 KEURIG, K-CUP, K-ROUNDS, ENVIRONMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIG CHANGE BREWING FOR K-CUPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEURIG INTRODUCING GREEN "K-ROUNDS"\par \par \uc2 KING, ACTOR, SON, IAN, GRIEF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REGINA KING OPENS UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON HER HEARTBREAK AFTER SON'S DEATH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SANTA ANA WINDS\par \par \uc2 MUNN, BREAST CANCER, MASTECTOMY, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OLIVIA MUNN REVEALS BREAST CANCER FIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTRESS SHARES HER DIAGNOSIS\par \par \uc2 KITCHENWARE, PURIFIER, CLEANERS, TILES, FLASHLIGHT\par \par \uc2 DUA LIPA, MURPHY, SWIFT, WEDDINGS\par \par \uc2 TRADER JOE'S, MINI TOTE, TIKTOK, TREND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRADER JOE'S MINI TOTE CRAZE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY ARE PEOPLE GOING NUTS FOR THIS MUST HAVE BAG?\par \par \uc2 FELLER, BUDGET, COOKING, RECIPES\par \par \uc2 WEIGHT LOSS, HEALTH, CHILDREN,\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSPIRING WEIGHT LOSS JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW ONE MAN LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...with some inspiration. This morning, we're sharing one person's inspiring health journey.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right, Sam. Everyone has their own motivation for losing weight, and one man chose to change his lifestyle in order to help fulfill his and his wife's dream of starting a family. Take a look at their story.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 I was always a little bit on the heavier side. The first time I can remember going on a diet was in the fourth grade. At my heaviest, I was 430 pounds.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For Isaiah Caldwell, weight has been a struggle his entire life. But it was the desire to start a family that finally motivated him to make a change.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 My wife and I were trying to get pregnant for a little over a year, and unfortunately, we were unable to, and I went into a doctor and found out that my weight may be playing a factor in that. So, after coming home from the doctor's office, I was terrified. I had tried to lose weight in the past, and I had failed at least three times. I started on a diet that I heard about on a podcast called the carnivore diet, looking delicious, and immediately started to see results. And weightlifting really became a hobby, something that I enjoyed and wanted to go to the gym for every day.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) His results were beyond just weight loss.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 My mental clarity was through the roof. I didn't have as much pain doing basic daily tasks. Even within a month of starting, my lipid panel looked phenomenal.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Isaiah's success has led him to encouraging others online.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 This weight loss journey has been one of the best decisions of my life. I feel better than ever, and I'm so hopeful for the future.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Isaiah is here with us. Isaiah, come on out. Yes, wow, what a transformation.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, sir. Come here. Look at you.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Love it, the before and after. Isaiah, welcome to "Good Morning America." It's so nice to see you.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 Thanks for having me.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Have a seat over here.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Congratulations, phenomenal.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Congratulations. You've made such a transformation, that before and after. What changes have you made in your life? How does it feel?\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 And there's been a lot of changes, but it feels incredible. I definitely don't regret it. It's one of the best decisions I've ever made in my life.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is hard work, though, and I know, whenever we're talking something medical, I want to get, you know, be very specific. So, you were engaged with your medical team throughout the process, it says here, and we recommend folks talk to their doctors before beginning a weight loss journey. But you followed what is called a carnivore diet. So, explain your process.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, out of the gate, I didn't really know how to lose weight. So, I just wanted to jump on a diet right then and there. When I came home from the doctor's office, I said, was listening to a podcast, heard about the carnivore diet, I'm just going to do it, see what happens and try to make a plan along the way. But you're right, blood work is really important, and it's motivating, too. When you see it going in the right direction, it makes you want to keep going.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I have so much compassion for you and your wife and everything you went through on the fertility journey. What changes were you thinking about making in your life, and why was that so important to you?\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. So, to give you a little backstory, you know, my wife and I, we had been trying for about a year, and we hadn't had any success. And going into the doctor's office, I was nervous that it had to do with my weight, but I didn't know. And once I found that out, I just kind of hit a rock-bottom moment. I felt I had done this to us, you know, even though naturally, it may not have been that. It may have been other factors. But I just knew that I wanted to do whatever it took to prove to myself that I did everything I could to rectify the situation.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Your story and the fact that you, you know, even your workouts became a hobby for you, it's just so, it lets people know what the key to success is. But we met Amanda in the commercial break, your wife, and she's standing right here. So, tell us how this actually, I know you're super proud of him, by the way. Did we get the, did we get the picture? Did we get the phone and picture of you guys?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, we took a picture of Amanda, but we need one of both of them after, in the commercial break.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, promise we will. So, tell us how this worked for your relationship.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 You know, it's amazing. My wife and I, we've always had a strong relationship. We've been married for eight years, and it's been phenomenal. But this process has really brought us closer together. I mean, she was my rock through the whole thing. She joined me on the exercises, on the diet. She did everything. I mean, obviously, you can tell, she's looking great, as well.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that smile says everything. It just really does.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, and it, and that shared hobby brought us together, you know. It was really cool. So, couples out there, if you're interested in losing weight together, I highly recommend it.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's a great partnership you have here, and it makes me understand why you want to be parents so much. And you're coming up on some big news tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 I hope so, yeah. I've got a test scheduled tomorrow. It's my next one. I haven't been tested in quite some time. So, we'll see if there's any improvement. But just so everyone knows, we're committed to becoming parents one way or another. We're happy to adopt or go down a different route. So, don't worry about us. I'm going to keep working if it doesn't come back positive, it'll be fine.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, we are, I'm so thrilled to hear that, that you're going to stay with that.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you'll let us know how it all goes, right? Because now, now I'm invested.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 We'll keep you updated.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Amanda, come over here, please. Please come over and give your wonderful husband a hug. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Come on.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are wishing you guys all the luck in the world with that test tomorrow and adoption and everything that's ahead for you.\par \par \uc2 ISAIAH CALDWELL (LOST MORE THAN 200 POUNDS)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. Thank you guys, I really appreciate.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, we appreciate you.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Are you two over there talking about vegetables?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Have a great day, everyone.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240403ek3e0000t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 March 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WINTER STORM, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WINTER BLAST SLAMMING WEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW, WIND & AVALANCHE ALERTS FROM CALIFORNIA TO COLORADO\par \par \uc2 BOEING, AMERICAN AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN AIRLINES FLIGHT MAKES EMERGENCY LANDING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LATEST INCIDE