 MURDER INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE SEARCH FOR MOTIVE AFTER ARREST OF SUSPECT IN 16-YEAR-OLD'S STABBING\par \par \uc2 CORCORAN, MORTGAGE, REAL ESTATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REAL ESTATE REALITY CHECK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BARBARA CORCORAN ON THE STATE OF THE HOUSING MARKET\par \par \uc2 GOLDEN GLOBE AWARDS, NOMINATIONS, "BARBENHEIMER"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "BARBENHEIMER" BLITZ!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOX OFFICE PHENOMENONS RULE THE GOLDEN GLOBE NOMINATIONS\par \par \uc2 NFL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, COX, LAW, EXCEPTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN LEAVES STATE FOR PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, COLD, WINTER, CHILLS, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BITTER COLD BLAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS WAKING UP TO WINTER-LIKE WIND CHILLS\par \par \uc2 GOOGLE\uc2 , ANDROID, APP, LAWSUIT, ANTI-TRUST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 GOOGLE\uc2  LOSES APP STORE LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JURY SAYS TECH GIANT VIOLATED ANTITRUST LAWS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to a federal jury ruling that \uc2 Google\uc2  violated anti-trust laws in running its Android app store. Elizabeth Schulze joins us now with how this will impact your phone and how "Fortnite" is involved. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Michael, and this is a case that could impact the price you pay when you download apps on your phone. A federal jury late Monday found \uc2 Google\uc2  guilty of having an illegal monopoly on its Android app store. And this is really the first major loss for \uc2 Google\uc2  as the tech giant faces several legal challenges over its dominance on the internet. Now, this case was brought by \uc2 Epic Games\uc2 , which is the creator of the popular videogame, "Fortnite."\u160\'00\'A0Epic accused \uc2 Google\uc2  of maintaining a monopoly on app store by charging companies fees when users make purchases from a game like "Fortnite." Epic's CEO writing, "Victory over \uc2 Google\uc2 , and free Fortnite," the company calling this decision a win for consumers.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Google\uc2  is vowing to appeal, saying that this trial actually made clear that we compete fiercely with \uc2 Apple\uc2  and its app store, as well as app stores on Android devices and gaming consoles. But ultimately, this decision could mean \uc2 Google\uc2  would have to change its business model so people who use those devices could find more apps there at lower prices, guys.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Elizabeth, thanks. Coming up on our "GMA Morning Menu," the mother who thought she had the flu, but it turned out to be a heart attack. She shares her message for all women.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, Jennifer Aniston opening up about Matthew Perry in a touching new interview.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, these health care workers are about to be part of one of the largest surprises on morning TV ever. And we're ready for "Wonka" week here on "GMA." We're going to talk to Willy Wonka himself, Timothee Chalamet, and his costar about their new movie and much more. And that's coming up right here on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Welcome back, everybody. There's a look at our holiday window display because it's\u160\'00\'A0time for our Advent calendar of deals. Every day this month, we're bringing you one special item as we count down to Christmas. And this morning, for day 12, our deal is compression pocket socks. They're between 50 to 62 percent off, and you can shop the assortment by scanning the QR code on the screen.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Sam, you need some.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I do. It's compression, and it has a pocket, George. And, of course, they're socks because I'm not wearing any right now anyway. That was the point.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That was the point, you're not wearing any socks.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, you know what George is getting you.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Thank you, George.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 All set.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240103ejcc0003c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS COURT DENIES EMERGENCY ABORTION PREGNANT MOTHER LEAVES STATE FOR PROCEDURE\b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, ZELENSKYY, FUNDING, BIDEN, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, WAR, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , BIDEN, NETANYAHU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS: ISRAEL STARTS FLOODING TUNNELS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, \uc2 COX\uc2 , WARNER, GAONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS COURT DENIES EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Meanwhile, back here in the US tonight, and to the deeply personal issue of abortion. And the young pregnant mother in Texas, her health in danger, unable to get an abortion because of the law in that state. And tonight, the Texas Supreme Court has now ruled against that mother and against the judge who said she should be allowed to get the abortion to protect her own health and to be able to have children in the future. So, what now? And how many women in other states are now facing the same fate? Again tonight, Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It was a first-of-its-kind case, a pregnant woman suing her state, requesting an emergency abortion. And now, the Texas Supreme Court ruling against 31-year-old Kate Cox, whose fetus had a severe condition and little chance of survival.\par \par \uc2 KATE COX (PLAINTIFF IN TEXAS SUPREME COURT CASE)\par \par \uc2 There's no outcome here, you know, that results in us taking home a healthy baby girl. So, it's, it's hard. It's overwhelming.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREGNANT MOTHER LEAVES STATE FOR PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Texas Supreme Court saying, she didn't qualify for the state's narrow exception, to prevent bodily harm or save the life of the mother. Stating, "No one disputes that Ms. Cox's pregnancy has been extremely complicated," but that some difficulties, even serious ones, "do not pose the heightened risks to the mother the exception encompasses." Cox going out of state for the procedure. Only 34 abortions have been recorded in Texas so far this year, compared to more than 50,000 in 2020 before that law went effect. Tonight, several states across the country now grappling with similar abortion restrictions.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA COURT CONSIDERS NEAR-TOTAL ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, Arizona's Supreme Court hearing arguments on whether to enact a century's old law that would abortion at any state of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 JAKE WARNER (SENIOR COUNSEL ALLIANCE DEFENDING FREEDOM)\par \par \uc2 For over 100 years, Arizona has fully protected life from the moment of conception.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW GAONA (ATTORNEY FOR PLANNED PARENTHOOD ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 Abortion is health care. And what that means is that this court's decision will have a profound impact on the ability of pregnant Arizonans to access that health care.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just moments ago, the President weighing in, calling what is playing out in Texas legal and medical chaos, saying no woman should be forced to go to court or flee her state to get access to health care, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott back with us here tonight. Rachel, thank you. And we should point out that Rachel is joining Diane Sawyer for an in-depth report on this deeply personal issue, and what many women are now facing.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON THE BRINK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IMPACT XC NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The report on "Impact x Nightline" called "On the Brink." Diane and Rachel uncovering the harrowing stories of pregnant women who have medical emergencies in states with laws restricting abortions, and the physicians caught in the middle.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It streams on \uc2 Hulu\uc2  beginning Thursday. Rachel, our thanks to you again tonight.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020231214ejcc0002w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE COURT HALTS RULING THAT WOULD HAVE ALLOWED WOMAN'S ABORTION\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADO, DEATHS, DAMAGE, RAIN, WINDS\par \par \uc2 BATTLE, \uc2 IDF\uc2 , GAZA, ASSAULT, WHO, PALESTINIANS\par \par \uc2 UNIVERSITIES, ANTI-SEMITISM, MAGILL, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DICTATOR, CAMPAIGN, CHENEY, BIDEN, POLL\par \par \uc2 HALEY, TRUMP, WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GAS, PRICES, AAA, TRAVEL, ROADS, FLIERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "SISTER ACT"\par \par \uc2 MEDINA, ARREST, MURDER, CHEERLEADER, SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 SHIVER, BAHAMAS, MURDER PLOT, LLOYD, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GIFT CARDS, SCAM, THIEVES, DUGGAN, VALDEPENA, RANDLE\par \par \uc2 NFL CHIEFS, BILLS, COWBOYS, EAGLES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FOR THE ROCKIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POTENTIAL SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the abortion battle in Texas. The State Supreme Court temporarily halted a ruling that would have allowed a woman to give what doctors call an emergency abortion.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT HALTS RULING THAT WOULD HAVE ALLOWED WOMAN'S ABORTION\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott is in Washington with those details for us. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, good morning. This has been whiplash for Kate Cox, the 31-year-old Texas woman at the center of this historic case. She is now waiting on the state's Supreme Court to weigh in to decide whether or not she can get an emergency abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Cox is 20 weeks pregnant. She was told by her doctors that her fetus has a severe condition and virtually no chance of survival. Her doctors also warn that the longer that she continues her pregnancy, the greater risk to her own personal health as well as her future fertility. So, she decided to sue the state of Texas. And in a stunning ruling, the judge sided with her, granting her permission to get that emergency abortion. But within hours, the state appealed that ruling, putting it on hold. Texas bans abortion outright, but there is a narrow exception to save the life of the mother. But this morning, the Texas attorney general is arguing that neither that severe condition that her fetus has or the future risk to her own fertility qualifies as an exception.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, the bottom line here, Kate Cox is now hanging in limbo. She's been to the emergency room four times within the last month. Her uterus is at risk of rupturing. And it's unclear when the State Supreme Court will weigh in, Linsey.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, a lot of people following this case, certainly far-reaching implications there. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240103ejcb0000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW HOPE FOR BREAST CANCER VACCINE? PHASE ONE TRIAL SHOWING PROMISING RESULTS\b0\par\par\uc2 856 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADO, DEATHS, DAMAGE, RAIN, WINDS\par \par \uc2 BATTLE, \uc2 IDF\uc2 , GAZA, ASSAULT, \uc2 WHO\uc2 , PALESTINIANS\par \par \uc2 UNIVERSITIES, ANTI-SEMITISM, MAGILL, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DICTATOR, CAMPAIGN, CHENEY, BIDEN, POLL\par \par \uc2 HALEY, TRUMP, WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GAS, PRICES, AAA, TRAVEL, ROADS, FLIERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "SISTER ACT"\par \par \uc2 MEDINA, ARREST, MURDER, CHEERLEADER, SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 SHIVER, BAHAMAS, MURDER PLOT, LLOYD, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GIFT CARDS, SCAM, THIEVES, DUGGAN, VALDEPENA, RANDLE\par \par \uc2 NFL CHIEFS, BILLS, COWBOYS, EAGLES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FOR THE ROCKIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POTENTIAL SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 MACY'S\uc2 , BUYOUT\par \par \uc2 EVERT, OVARIAN CANCER, GARDNER\par \par \uc2 HOWARD, WEIGHT LOSS, GULLET\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMPANION PRODUCTS FOR WEIGHT LOSS DRUGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR MOVE FROM BIG FOOD COMPANIES LIKE NESTLE & \uc2 GENERAL MILLS\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW HOPE FOR BREAST CANCER VACCINE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PHASE ONE TRIAL SHOWING PROMISING RESULTS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A promising new breast cancer vaccine trial out of \uc2 Cleveland Clinic\uc2 . Approximately one in eight women here in the US are expected to develop breast cancer in their life time. Our chief medical correspondent Dr. Jennifer Ashton is going to tell us about this phase 1.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But you want to make it clear. That a vaccine, we're talking years down the line.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But can you just explain to folks the concept behind the vaccine?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. So, for breast cancer, yeah, we're talking years down the road. But the concept of immunotherapy, let's do a little mini med school. First of all, when someone develops cancer, why doesn't the immune system attack that tumor, seeing it as foreign? The reason is because it comes from our own cells, right? So, it kind of flies under our surveillance radar. Using the concept of immunotherapy now, there are clinical trials in progress that take a snippet from a person's actual tumor and then kind of fold it into, in a lot of cases, mRNA vaccine technology. So, it lets that loose, so that the peon's immune system can actually fight its own cancer. We already have a couple vaccines against cancer. We have a cervical cancer vaccine. We have a liver cancer vaccine against hepatitis B. And there's a vaccine that's \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved to treat metastatic prostate cancer. But for breast cancer, there is a lot of exciting research ongoing.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, what does this latest data showing you?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. So, let me talk you through this latest breast cancer vaccine phase 1 clinical trials.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER VACCINE TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PHASE 1 CLINICAL TRIAL, 16 PATIENTS\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 So, it really is looking at safety here. Looked at 16 patients with triple negative breast cancer. They found that in 75% of those patients they achieved a good immune response. There were no safety signals reported. Remember, that's the purpose and point with a phase 1 clinical trial. So, and this is not the only one for breast cancer. Could, I want to emphasize, could potentially start to be available in about five years or so.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You mentioned immunotherapy a little bit. And that's so encouraging for a lot of folks.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But what are, just remind us how we can prevent the risk of breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER PREVENTION & DETECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU CAN HELP BEAT THE DISEASE\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, you want to shift the focus from treatment to risk reduction. And when you're talking about breast cancer, the key things, a lot are behavioral.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WAYS TO REDUCE RISK OF BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Limiting or avoiding alcohol completely, not smoking, keeping your weight in a healthy range and exercising. And breastfeeding, if possible, has been shown to be associated with a lower risk. This is not, I repeat, not to say that any woman who gets breast cancer is to blame.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But there is a lot that you can do in your control to lower your risk.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you for saying that, as somebody who had it.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You bet.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But you do. You think like, what did I do? What did I do? And you know sometimes...\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A lot of times, nothing. You did nothing wrong. But you can have a lot of control.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. All right. Yeah, but so many promising things that are out there right now.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, exciting.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll see you on "GMA3."\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, you will, my friend.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240103ejcb0000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS WOMAN LEAVES STATE FOR ABORTION ATTYS: HEALTH DETERIORATING; FORCED TO FLEE STATE\b0\par\par\uc2 528 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BUILDING, COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, SUPREME COURT, SMITH, IMMUNITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCOTUS AGREES TO CONSIDER SMITH REQUEST\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, DUANE, \uc2 COX\uc2 , GUERRA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS WOMAN LEAVES STATE FOR ABORTION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the meantime, we turn to the issue of abortion tonight, and the deeply personal case involving a young pregnant mother in Texas. She and her husband have been fighting to get her an abortion. Her doctors say her health is at risk. But authorities told the family the law prohibits it. The judge who then decided the woman can move ahead with an abortion only to have the Texas state Supreme Court step in to block any abortion for now. So, what that young mother says she's been forced to do instead. Here's Rachel Scott tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ATTYS: HEALTH DETERIORATING; FORCED TO FLEE STATE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the 31-year-old Texas woman at the center of that unprecedented case, suing the state for an emergency abortion, now leaving Texas for the procedure. The attorneys for Kate Cox saying her health is on the line and she couldn't wait for the Texas Supreme Court to weigh in.\par \par \uc2 MOLLY DUANE\uc2  (SENIOR STAFF ATTORNEY CENTER FOR REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS)\par \par \uc2 Kate was in an out of the hospital multiple times over the last month. This is time sensitive, critical health care that shouldn't be hampered by laws and policies.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kate, a mother of two from Dallas, now more than 20 weeks pregnant, had been told by doctors that her fetus had a severe abnormality and little chance of survival and that continuing the pregnancy could put her health at risk, possibly preventing her from getting pregnant again. Texas now bans abortions outright with one narrow exception, to prevent major bodily harm or save the life of the mother. Kate told me she was certain that would apply to her.\par \par \uc2 KATE COX (SEEKING EMERGENCY ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I could see in this case, surely, I would qualify for that exemption.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just days ago, a judge siding with Kate, granting permission to get an abortion.\par \par \uc2 JUDGE MAYA GUERRA (TRAVIS COUNTY TEXAS)\par \par \uc2 I am going to grant the temporary restraining order.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kate wiping away tears. But a day later, the Texas Supreme Court temporarily halted that ruling in response to an appeal by the Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , who said the "fatal fetal condition does not meet the medical exception." Her attorneys saying it left Kate with no choice but to travel to a state where she can legally obtain an abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The lawyers for Kate Cox have not revealed which state she is traveling to, but they told the Texas Supreme Court they plan to move forward with that case. They are expecting more women to be put in this same scenario, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rachel Scott, who's been following this case very closely for us. Thank you, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020231213ejcb00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 100 DISNEY WISHES\b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 INFANT MORTALITY, HEALTH CARE, DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 HANUKKAH, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PILO, KEIDAR\par \par \uc2 PRICE, NYBERG, GARCIA, QUIMBY, ESCOBAR, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE PEOPLE FEEDING THE PEOPLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW THE HOUSTON FOOD BANK PROVIDES "FOOD FOR BETTER LIVES"\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "HOW THE GRINCH STOLE CHRISTMAS"\par \par \uc2 "WONKA", CHALAMET, COLMAN\par \par \uc2 GIFT WRAPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL IT? WON'T IT?\par \par \uc2 DISNEY\uc2 , ANNIVERSARY, MAKE-A-WISH FOUNDATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 100 DISNEY WISHES\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Some \uc2 Disney\uc2  magic. "GMA" is teaming up with \uc2 Disney\uc2  and \uc2 Make-A-Wish Foundation\uc2  to celebrate the power of 100 wishes. This morning, the countdown continues with wish number 50. Nine-year-old Carter has been suffering from medical issues since he was just 4 months old and wished to go to Disney World.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Well, Carter got a special meet and greet with his favorite \uc2 Disney\uc2  hero Moana. And a big surprise for Carter and his family, a private visit to the new Moana attraction in EPCOT before it even opened to the public. We will be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000by\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 483 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 INFANT MORTALITY, HEALTH CARE, DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 HANUKKAH, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PILO, KEIDAR\par \par \uc2 PRICE, NYBERG, GARCIA, QUIMBY, ESCOBAR, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE PEOPLE FEEDING THE PEOPLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW THE HOUSTON FOOD BANK PROVIDES "FOOD FOR BETTER LIVES"\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "HOW THE GRINCH STOLE CHRISTMAS"\par \par \uc2 "WONKA", CHALAMET, COLMAN\par \par \uc2 GIFT WRAPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL IT? WON'T IT?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's go back to Somara for another check of the weather. Somara?\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Can I get that, without having a dog? Like, is that weird?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No. Dog included.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why not?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. All right, so let's take a look at this threat. Northeast, I hope you have a plan B for your Sundays specifically. We're looking at flood watches from Portland, Maine down to DC, up to three inches of rain possible.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIMING THE STORM\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Timing out this storm system. So, by 10:00 AM, it's riding through Atlanta, bringing in the threat for storms. And then, along the I-95 corridor, it really hits hard by tomorrow evening around 6:00 PM. If you look further inland, West Virginia, Pennsylvania, upstate New York, we've got inland snow. Lake effect snow only enhancing this, but the heaviest of the rain moving into New England by Monday morning. Very gusty conditions as well, anywhere from one to two inches.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAINFALL FORECAST\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we could see amounts as high as three inches of rain for your Sunday. That's a look at the forecast across the country, let's see what's going on in your neighborhood.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bx\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY FDA APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FDA\uc2  APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the big news in treating sickle cell disease. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approving two types of gene therapies. And ABC's Melissa Adan joins us now with more on that. Melissa, good morning.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Whit. It's pretty remarkable. Look, the President supporting the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of the first two breakthrough therapies for sickle cell disease.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, some researchers really calling the treatment a functional cure for many patients. Sickle cell is a genetic condition that affects approximately 100,000 Americans, primarily black Americans with African ancestry and Hispanic Americans. One of the new treatments will use a gene-editing technique called CRISPR, the first approval of its kind. And the other uses an older gene therapy, which has the ability to remove and replace highly specific sections of DNA.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The process is difficult and expensive with patients undergoing chemotherapy to prepare, which may even jeopardize fertility. But an encouraging sign is patients will only need to receive the treatment just once over the course of their lifetime. And that's really raising hopes for treating other diseases. Gio?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) An encouraging sign indeed. All right, Melissa, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bn\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE PEOPLE FEEDING THE PEOPLE HOW THE HOUSTON FOOD BANK PROVIDES "FOOD FOR BETTER LIVES\b0\par\par\uc2 1,034 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FDA\uc2  APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 INFANT MORTALITY, HEALTH CARE, DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 HANUKKAH, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PILO, KEIDAR\par \par \uc2 PRICE, NYBERG, GARCIA, QUIMBY, ESCOBAR, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE PEOPLE FEEDING THE PEOPLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW THE HOUSTON FOOD BANK PROVIDES "FOOD FOR BETTER LIVES"\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And turning now to our series, "Serving Up Kindness." And this morning, we are highlighting the \uc2 Houston Food Bank\uc2 . In terms of distribution, it's actually the largest food bank in the United States with more than 1,600 partner agencies. And their mission is simple, providing food for better lives.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The healing reach of the \uc2 Houston Food Bank\uc2  is vast and life-changing.\par \par \uc2 VOLUNTEER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Thank you. Be blessed.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Each year, serving more than 120 million nutritious meals throughout southeast Texas, some getting those meals right here at the First Missionary Baptist Church of Houston.\par \par \uc2 VOLUNTEER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Right now, we are in need for canned goods, breads, cereal.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For Joyce Price, a church member who's raising her five grandkids, it's a critical life line as she told our ABC station \uc2 KTRK\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JOYCE PRICE (FOOD BANK CLIENT)\par \par \uc2 The groceries that are out here is ridiculously high. You still have to buy them clothes, socks, underwear. The food bank has helped because it lessens the grocery bill for me. You don't have to struggle as hard with the food decisions. We're grateful.\par \par \uc2 VOLUNTEER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 All right, go get your green bag.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the \uc2 Houston Food Bank\uc2  is determined to meet the need wherever it is. Their Backpack Buddy Program allows parents of students to ask for help.\par \par \uc2 SAMANTHA NYBERG (SCHOOL COUNSELOR HUFFMAN MIDDLE SCHOOL)\par \par \uc2 Every week, students receive a bag of food from the \uc2 Houston Food Bank\uc2 . Students are able to grab the green bag and either put it in their own backpack or we supply perfectly brand-new backpacks for them to carry home food for the weekend.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And at \uc2 Sam Houston State University\uc2 , the food bank helps stock this food pantry, allowing students to focus on studies rather than worrying about filling their stomachs.\par \par \uc2 KAYLA GARCIA (GRAD STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 Transitioning from my parents, I had to start taking on a lot of responsibilities on my own, whether it was bills, payments for groceries and things like that, it was very difficult.\par \par \uc2 IAN QUIMBY (JUNIOR)\par \par \uc2 Freshmen sometimes they're still not able to afford groceries.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Some of the students receiving this aid stocking shelves, so others can benefit.\par \par \uc2 JHONATHAN ESCOBAR (SENIOR)\par \par \uc2 With the money I save, I can use that towards my education now.\par \par \uc2 LYDIA WILLIAMS (SENIOR)\par \par \uc2 Without the support of the food bank, I might not have made it this far through college. And I'm just very grateful for everything they've done for me.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Some incredible humans right there.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the \uc2 Houston Food Bank\uc2  is doing amazing things in their community, of course. They're able to provide meals in 18 counties. So much of that incredible work made possible by the generosity of donors and volunteers, which they say is one of the biggest needs right now. They need more volunteers.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No one should go hungry in this country. No one.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly. People making a huge difference. And, Gio, you've been involved in this series for a while. And this week, you met Seal Witherspoon (PH) from \uc2 City Harvest\uc2 . She's one of their superstar volunteers. And you gave her a big surprise to help her get to work. Let's take a look at that.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, you do the bike, right?\par \par \uc2 VOLUNTEER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I bike.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Don't you think it's time for some new wheels? Let's bring out the wheels. We got to give Seal a brand-new bike. It's yours. It's yours to get there safely in style. Oh. This is yours.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What a beautiful moment.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I've seen that a few times now. And every time, it gets me. So appreciative.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She is so special. She was so appreciative, but it's also the work that she does.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She was actually in that line herself getting food once upon a time. Now, she's giving her time to do that and she gets there on that bike. It's really powerful.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And part of those tears you could tell, it's not about her getting a bike, it means that she can do more for other people. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For other people. Yes.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. Absolutely. Thank you, Seal.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000br\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ETHAN CRUMBLEY SENTENCED TO LIFE WITHOUT PAROLE TEEN PLEADED GUILTY TO KILLING FOUR STUDENTS IN 2021 SCHOOL SHOOTING\b0\par\par\uc2 526 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just so much pain two months in. All right, Tom, thank you so much. Now we're gonna turn to teen school shooter Ethan Crumbley sentenced to life in prison without parole for killing four students at a Michigan school. ABC's Morgan Norwood joins us with that, and Morgan, the victims' families were in court. It was an emotional day.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ETHAN CRUMBLEY SENTENCED TO LIFE WITHOUT PAROLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEEN PLEADED GUILTY TO KILLING FOUR STUDENTS IN 2021 SCHOOL SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Gio, good morning. That's right, so emotional. Life without parole. And it was Ethan Crumbley's calculated planning, execution style killings, and the anguish lamented in court by more than two dozen that led the Judge to that maximum punishment.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXT OF DIALOGUE\par \par \uc2 JUDGE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Life without the possibility of parole.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, Ethan Crumbley, the Michigan teenager behind the 2021 mass school shooting that killed four of his classmates and injured seven others, beginning a lifelong prison sentence. The Judge, handing down the maximum punishment, describing Ethan as being obsessed with violence, stalking the hallways, pick and choosing who was going to die.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EMOTIONAL VICTIMS' STATEMENTS DURING SENTENCING HEARING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRUMBLEY GIVEN LIFE IN PRISON WITHOUT THE POSSIBILITY OF PAROLE\par \par \uc2 BUCK MYRE (FATHER OF TATE MYRE)\par \par \uc2 We are miserable. We miss Tate. Our family has a permanent hole in it that can never be fixed, ever.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Before learning his fate, Crumbley facing the families impacted by his deadly rampage at Oxford High School. And one by one, the parents and loved ones of Madisyn Baldwin, Tate Myre, Hana St. Juliana, and Justin Shilling describing the anguish of losing their children and family members.\par \par \uc2 CRYSTAL BALDWIN (LOVED ONE OF SHOOTING VICTIM)\par \par \uc2 In that moment my whole world stopped. I heard the words and froze as if the world was spinning and I was standing still. Then came the cries and screaming from Madisyn's parents.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Crumbley, who was 15 at the time of the shooting, pleaded guilty last year to 24 charges including first-degree premeditated murder and terrorism causing death. Prosecutors say he carefully planned out the attack. After hearing from nearly 30 family members, survivors and witnesses, Crumbley addressing the court.\par \par \uc2 ETHAN CRUMBLEY (CONVICTED OF MURDER)\par \par \uc2 I really am sorry, what I've done, what I've taken of them.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Ethan's parents, Jennifer and James Crumbley also face charges in that mass shooting, accused of giving their son easy access to that semiautomatic gun and dismissing signs that he was a threat. Whit?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000b9\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Let's turn it over to Somara Theodore for a check of the weather now. Hey, Somara.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIMING THE STORM\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey. I hope you don't have any big East Coast plans here on Sunday because we're looking at a washout. Out in the Midwest already starting to get that rain machine growing. Glazed roads there in Chicago from the rain. And the flood threat is really hyper concentrated Sunday into Monday. We could see up to three inches of rain falling from the DMV, Washington, DC area up into New England. So, notice the timing on this, right? So, this is Sunday am, some storms roll through Atlanta, and then we really get hit hard in the Northeast between about four into 4:00 pm tomorrow, into the overnight hours.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAINFALL FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOWFALL FORECAST\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If you look back on the west side of I-95, we've got some inland snow there and some lake effect snow that will be enhancing this through states like Pennsylvania, Ohio and Upstate New York, very gusty conditions as well. Okay, so totals, one to two inches a little further inland. Right where the I-95 corridor is sitting, we could see anywhere from two to three inches of rain. So, this rain is coming down quick and hard. And then, as far as snowfall goes, they've already been hit pretty hard in states like Vermont and New Hampshire, and they could see up to 15 inches of snow. That's a look at your forecast. Let's see what's going on a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS IS GMA\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And so, for my friends in the northeast, everything needs to get done today because by tomorrow conditions will deteriorate quickly, so I'd be inside with some hot cocoa.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sounds good.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bd\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "THE FROZEN RIVER" AUTHOR ARIEL LAWHON TALKS GMA'S DECEMBER BOOK CLUB PICK\b0\par\par\uc2 1,047 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 INFANT MORTALITY, HEALTH CARE, DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 HANUKKAH, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PILO, KEIDAR\par \par \uc2 PRICE, NYBERG, GARCIA, QUIMBY, ESCOBAR, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE PEOPLE FEEDING THE PEOPLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW THE HOUSTON FOOD BANK PROVIDES "FOOD FOR BETTER LIVES"\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "HOW THE GRINCH STOLE CHRISTMAS"\par \par \uc2 "WONKA", CHALAMET, COLMAN\par \par \uc2 GIFT WRAPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL IT? WON'T IT?\par \par \uc2 DISNEY\uc2 , ANNIVERSARY, MAKE-A-WISH FOUNDATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 100 DISNEY WISHES\par \par \uc2 "THE FROZEN RIVER"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "THE FROZEN RIVER"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTHOR ARIEL LAWHON TALKS GMA'S DECEMBER BOOK CLUB PICK\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now to this month's "GMA Book Club" pick. "The Frozen River" is the latest from "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 " best-selling author Ariel Lawhon. And it is a historical mystery inspired by the life and diary of an 18th century midwife. Ariel, welcome to "GMA."\par \par \uc2 ARIEL LAWHON (AUTHOR "THE FROZEN RIVER")\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much for having me.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was just telling you that I love reading first lines. And yours is, "The body floats downstream." I'm in. I'm so in with this. Tell me about this because Martha's story, the midwife we're just talking about, you found out about the story at your doctor's office.\par \par \uc2 ARIEL LAWHON (AUTHOR "THE FROZEN RIVER")\par \par \uc2 Yes, I was pregnant with my fourth son and I was waiting for my doctor. And had he not been late to my appointment, this book would have never been written.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 ARIEL LAWHON (AUTHOR "THE FROZEN RIVER")\par \par \uc2 So, I stuck it out and I waited for him and read everything that was left in the office and was finally down to this pamphlet. And it told the story of a woman named Martha Ballard, a midwife in the 1700s, who had delivered over a thousand babies in her career, but never lost a mother. And my own doctor, at the time, couldn't boast a record like that. And I remember thinking, that would make a great novel. So, I ripped the page out and stuck it in my purse and took it home.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's amazing where ideas come from.\par \par \uc2 ARIEL LAWHON (AUTHOR "THE FROZEN RIVER")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But you waited for this one because you have all your other books. This one was, what, your sixth novel?\par \par \uc2 ARIEL LAWHON (AUTHOR "THE FROZEN RIVER")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why did you wait so long?\par \par \uc2 ARIEL LAWHON (AUTHOR "THE FROZEN RIVER")\par \par \uc2 At the time, I just thought I wasn't ready. In hindsight, I think I needed more time under my belt as a mother. The main character in this book is 54 years old. She's a mature woman and her children are mostly grown. And in hindsight, I think I just needed to have my kids grow up a little bit as well.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, I love that. Okay, so you're known, of course, for writing historical fiction with very strong women leads. And we partner, of course, with Little Free Library to get copies of "GMA Book Club" picks to readers all across the US. And this morning, I want you to look at this because one of our stewards, Mary Buck from Kennewick, Washington, has a question for you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "THE FROZEN RIVER", ARIEL LAWHON\par \par \uc2 LITTLE FREE LIBRARY STEWARD (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 How do you balance staying true to historical events while creating compelling characters and narratives? And are there any specific challenges in, that you faced in this genre?\par \par \uc2 ARIEL LAWHON (AUTHOR "THE FROZEN RIVER")\par \par \uc2 That's a good question. Thank you. For historical fiction, I think the trick is you have to stay true to the facts as recorded in history. But I look for the story itself in between, in the cracks, the conversations that weren't recorded, the betrayals that no one knows about. And the challenge even then is, if you have a book set 200 years in the past, my job is to make it feel close. I have to remove the distance. I have to make it feel like you're living it now, not like something that happened a long time ago.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, we cannot wait to dive in. Thank you so much, Ariel, we so appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 ARIEL LAWHON (AUTHOR "THE FROZEN RIVER")\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we'll be right back. You remember, you can scan that QR ode for the book, "The Frozen River." It's available right now. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, get more "GMA" in your day with "GMA" live streaming on ABC News Live this morning. And Whit is on "World News Tonight."\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, yes. You're back.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're back. We're back for one night only.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) One night only.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sports hiatus. We'll see you tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bz\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HANUKKAH CELEBRATIONS IN ISRAEL DISPLACED JEWS FIND LIGHT IN DARK TIMES\b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 INFANT MORTALITY, HEALTH CARE, DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 HANUKKAH, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PILO, KEIDAR\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, marks the third night of Hanukkah, the Jewish festival of light, celebrating the triumph of light over darkness.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HANUKKAH CELEBRATIONS IN ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DISPLACED JEWS FIND LIGHT IN DARK TIMES\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And this year, during the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war, the holiday is more meaningful than ever. ABC's Ines de la Cuetara is in Jerusalem with more. Hi there, Ines.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Erielle. And this year, the first night of Hanukkah also marking the two-month anniversary of the war as families here continue mourning loved ones and praying for the safe return of the hostages.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The lighting of a candle marking the start of Hanukkah just two months after one of the darkest days in Israel's history. In kibbutz Be'eri, at least 89 residents were killed and at least 27 were still being held hostage. The survivors, still living in temporary housing, coming together to mark the eight-day Jewish festival.\par \par \uc2 PEARCH PILO (SURVIVOR BE'ERI KIBBUTZ)\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, my son come over and showed me, mom, I found it.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This Hanukkiah, a special candle holder, one of the few things she was able to salvage from what's left of her home.\par \par \uc2 PEARCH PILO (SURVIVOR BE'ERI KIBBUTZ)\par \par \uc2 It's a part of my life. I have almost nothing. I went out with my underwear and nothing, barefoot and I have nothing. I got this yesterday, it's just unbelievable.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At the Wailing Wall in Jerusalem, the holiest site in Judaism, groups locking arms, singing and praying.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HANUKKAH IN WARTIME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING THE FESTIVAL OF LIGHTS DESPITE THE DARKNESS\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While 138 candles were lit in Tel Aviv, one for each of the remaining hostages. The festival of lights celebrated from Kyiv to Berlin, all the way to the space station.\par \par \uc2 ASTRONAUT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Happy Hanukkah.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In the US, Menorahs lit from New York to Washington, even as some events were scaled back or altogether canceled amid the rise in antisemitism.\par \par \uc2 ELAD KEIDAR (SURVIVOR BE'ERI KIBBUTZ)\par \par \uc2 I think this is one of the main things of Hanukkah, it unites everybody.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Elad Keidar's two parents were murdered by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . His father used to build the kibbutz's menorahs. And he'd be pleased, he says, to see the kibbutz beginning to pick up the pieces.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And people we've been speaking to telling us this is the saddest Hanukkah in the history of Israel as the war enters its third month, and this week seeing some of the most intense fighting to date. Erielle?\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ines, thank you. Hoping the light can drive out darkness in this fractured world.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, absolutely. A powerful story. Thank you, Ines.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bq\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WILL IT? WON'T IT? GIFT-WRAPPING HACKS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,502 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 INFANT MORTALITY, HEALTH CARE, DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 HANUKKAH, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PILO, KEIDAR\par \par \uc2 PRICE, NYBERG, GARCIA, QUIMBY, ESCOBAR, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE PEOPLE FEEDING THE PEOPLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW THE HOUSTON FOOD BANK PROVIDES "FOOD FOR BETTER LIVES"\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "HOW THE GRINCH STOLE CHRISTMAS"\par \par \uc2 "WONKA", CHALAMET, COLMAN\par \par \uc2 GIFT WRAPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL IT? WON'T IT?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm so jealous of Will Ganss' outfit today and Archie and the whole thing.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Archie.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let me get to it in a minute. We're back with our series of "Will It or Won't It" with a giant Will Ganss head behind us. And it's the season for giving. And this morning, Will Ganss joins us testing out the top tips for wrapping oddly shaped presents and highlighting some of those popular items that sort of pop up and gift his holiday season. Important stuff.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right. I wish I could help with the outfit, but I can't. I can help you with wrapping paper hacks because that hashtag has 31 million views on TikTok this holiday season. So, if your decoration skills are strong, and your caroling croon something a slay, maybe it's time to level up your wrapping paper game. This holiday season, I'm becoming a wrapper.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MUSIC VIDEO, "THE REAL SLIM SHADY"\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Not that kind, this kind.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Putting some of TikTok's most popular wrapping paper hacks to the test. First up, how to wrap something bulky like a stuffed animal. Ends, top and bottom all meet in the middle. Slide your gift inside and finish the bag.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Will it or won't it? In this case, it won't. In a world in which gift bags already exist and, yes, that's the world that we live in, just go buy a gift bag. It's going to hold up a lot better, it's going to save you some time and your print is not going to be upside down.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, to the candy wrapper hack, useful for wrapping smaller items like a candle or a pair of socks using scrapbook paper. Fold it over three times and twice more at the ends.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Make sure you have a strong pair of scissors for this next part. You're going to cut not all the way to a point but close to one.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tape your rectangle together, slide your gift inside and tie the ends ribbons.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Will it or won't it work? In this case, it will. I think it looks pretty cute.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And finally, how to wrap an article of clothing when you don't have a box. After measuring out your paper and folding over the edges on either side, start building a massive envelope.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rookie mistake, not investing in the double-sided tape.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But will it or won't it?\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm going to say it won't. Who wants this sitting under the tree? That last one was a little tough to look at. And let me just say that those content creators, though, they do make those wrapping paper hacks work like a charm. But for me, my time and my Christmas skill set is more suited to shopping for gifts instead of wrapping for gifts, which brings us here.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It sure does. Okay. So, now that we know the top wrapping hacks, we've got something to gift wrap here. These are the trendiest gifts out there according to \uc2 Google\uc2  that you might want to wrap this holiday season. So, what do we have?\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's exactly right. Thanks to insight from \uc2 Google\uc2 , we're highlighting some of the hottest items to shop, to gift this holiday season. The trending searches throughout the year are right here and they're all shoppable, just scan the QR code on your screen to go to these items.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, great stocking stuffer, first up.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, this is the claw clip. So, like, I love how everything old is new again.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRENDING GIFTS TOP SHOP THIS SEASON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLAW CLIPS\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, it's giving '90s girl energy. But they're very, very hot right now.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) My daughters love these.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really matches. It matches my whole outfit.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Interest reached, yeah, it does, an all-time high on \uc2 Google\uc2  this past year. These from \uc2 Lululemon\uc2  come in various shapes, sizes and colors, as you can see. And they're all online starting at just 18 bucks.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. So, this one here, this was searched more this year than ever before. Tell us about this. A puzzle vase?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUZZLE VASES\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. It's a puzzle vase. So, I got very into puzzles during the pandemic. But I'm not to this level yet. But I think it is a cool way to elevate your puzzle game. And if you're going to spend time with your family over the holidays, it's a good way to kind of do something together. They're all online right now starting at $46.99.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's like therapeutic to put together puzzles, but also therapeutic candles. So, these are a good hostess gift, host or hostess gift that you recommend.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDLE WARMERS\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Candles themselves are so 2022. 2023, we're talking about candle warmers. All right?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, this is really, really great. And over 1,000% increase in searches on \uc2 Google\uc2  this past year. These candle warmers are very chic.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Very chic. But what do we need these for? What do they do? They just warm your candles, bring the essence to life.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They warm your candle, so they diffuse the scent without, like, having to burn the candle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Having to light it. That's really great.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly. These are fantastic, starting at $49.99.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, according to \uc2 Google\uc2  now, popular for your pet.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Popular for your pet and yourself.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this is a good stocking stuffer. Right?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUMAN-DOG BEDS\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Depending on how big your stocking is I guess that's true. So, what's really trending this year is a human dog bed combo. So, you can cuddle with your dog, put on a movie. Archie is going to (inaudible) comfortable.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Archie is loving it. He's got to have a dig.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Up 1,600% this year. I would be very happy to see this under the tree. Online, starting at $179.99, which is a little pricey but you can't put a price tag on that.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Love it. Archie is going to spin around a few more times before he gets comfortable. Thank you, Will. All right and, of course, you can just scan the QR code on the screen.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bw\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TALKING WITH THE CAST OF "WONKA" NEW MOVIE ABOUT THE ICONIC CHARACTER WILLY WONKA\b0\par\par\uc2 1,582 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 INFANT MORTALITY, HEALTH CARE, DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 HANUKKAH, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PILO, KEIDAR\par \par \uc2 PRICE, NYBERG, GARCIA, QUIMBY, ESCOBAR, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE PEOPLE FEEDING THE PEOPLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW THE HOUSTON FOOD BANK PROVIDES "FOOD FOR BETTER LIVES"\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "HOW THE GRINCH STOLE CHRISTMAS"\par \par \uc2 "WONKA", CHALAMET, COLMAN\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to a sweet new movie, "Wonka" is the story of how iconic character Willy Wonka became a chocolate maker.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TALKING WITH THE CAST OF "WONKA"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW MOVIE ABOUT THE ICONIC CHARACTER WILLY WONKA\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's got a star-studded cast. And our own Maggie Rulli talked with some of the cast. And she is now in London. Hey, good morning, Mags, good assignment.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Erielle, good morning. Yeah, so this assignment and this movie were definitely sweet. Most of the sets on "Wonka" were edible, including elaborate chocolate teacups and every special Wonka chocolate bite that you see. The cast says, though, they never got sick of it. And after working on "Wonka," their sweet tooth is stronger than ever.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "WILLY WONKA AND THE CHOCOLATE FACTORY"\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Gene Wilder captured our imaginations in "Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory."\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "CHARLIE AND THE CHOCOLATE FACTORY"\par \par \uc2 JOHNNY DEPP (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 And you, well, you're just lucky to be here, aren't you?\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Johnny Depp delighted us in "Charlie and the Chocolate Factory." But the story of how the eccentric chocolatier found success in the candy world has yet to be told, until now.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "WONKA"\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 You see, I'm something of a magician, inventor and chocolate maker.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Starring Timothee Chalamet as a young Wonka.\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 No, quiet up and listen down. Nope, scratch that. Reverse it.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was it like when you put on that burgundy velvet jacket for the first time?\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Well, it was exciting. It was a dream come true, and it was a lot of pressure because people are very protective over characters they love and films they love. But like you said, it's a new story. This is a story of a young hopeful, cheery, ambitious, happy-eyed, maybe naive young man trying to achieve his dreams.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Timothee surrounded by a golden ticket cast, Hugh Grant, Olivia Colman, Rowan Atkinson, Keegan-Michael Key, Calah Lane, and Sally Hawkins.\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 May I present Willy Wonka's Wild and Wonderful Wishy-Washy Wonka Walker. Please, don't make me say that again.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was it like working together?\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 It's a big laugh.\par \par \uc2 KEEGAN-MICHAEL KEY ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 It was a big laugh, yeah.\par \par \uc2 CALAH LANE ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA COLMAN ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Fun.\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 A lot of joy.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA COLMAN ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. And Calah, whenever you answered this question, you said it was like a family.\par \par \uc2 CALAH LANE ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA COLMAN ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Such a lovely thing to say, but it did, it did feel like that.\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Wonka family, and we'd all gather and hang out except for Hugh, who didn't want to hang out.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is that true?\par \par \uc2 HUGH GRANT ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Absolutely true.\par \par \uc2 KEEGAN-MICHAEL KEY ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 You're going to get more than a bonk on the head.\par \par \uc2 KEEGAN-MICHAEL KEY ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Part of the reason I took the role is because I wanted to work with him so badly. And I think he is...\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 KEEGAN-MICHAEL KEY ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 I just love you and love your talent.\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Thank you. Same here. And I was dying to work with Keegan because I've grown up on his work.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Timothee shimmying into his first musical role.\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 I've been out for a bit. I'll be back before roll call.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was that like to be able to sing and dance?\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 It was totally different skill set and it made me, you know, just, I was already very admiring of Fred Astaire. When you do a war movie or something, you know it's going to be physically challenging, but it was, you know, if you're doing 13 takes of a dance number.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Olivia Colman says taking on the sour Mrs. Scrubbit was a real treat.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was so fun about that character was just how horrible she is.\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look, I love that face. Did you have fun playing someone?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA COLMAN ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 I loved it. I love being a baddy.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was so fun about it?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA COLMAN ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 When you read it, it's pretty obvious that way she talked. And really, it's just so much fun, it's much, much more fun the play a baddy.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA COLMAN ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Thank you. That'll do.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Left the theater with this huge smile on my face singing. But there were parts of the film where I started to cry. But both the women next to me were also dabbing their eyes, so I felt like we were in it together.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA COLMAN ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I looked at my husband, I looked sideways.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Did he cry?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA COLMAN ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 And he was like.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No.\par \par \uc2 KEEGAN-MICHAEL KEY ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Oh, really?\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Who else had some tears during the premiere?\par \par \uc2 KEEGAN-MICHAEL KEY ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 I did.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You did?\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Oh, yeah.\par \par \uc2 KEEGAN-MICHAEL KEY ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I did, especially the music really hooks you emotionally.\par \par \uc2 CALAH LANE ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 KEEGAN-MICHAEL KEY ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 The music has so much heart to it. Yeah, I had, I had them streaming down a few times.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) "Wonka," a story of an unwavering dreamer.\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 He's sort like a phoenix rising the whole movie because he's constantly told no, he's constantly being rejected and crumbling, and immediately has a new idea or a new ambition and won't take no for an answer.\par \par \uc2 TIMOTHEE CHALAMET ("WONKA")\par \par \uc2 I guess it's time to change the world.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And "Wonka" hits theaters next Friday, December 15th. But you guys just got a sneak peek at some of those dance numbers. Timothee actually told us, this was the most physically exhausting role he's ever been in. That some of those dance sequences took at least 13 takes if not more. But I have to say, for me, forever and always, the most iconic dance from "Wonka" is the Oompa-Loompa dance. And I did ask Hugh Grant to do the dance for us and he said no. He pretty much shot me down immediately.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Shocked to hear that.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We were hoping. We were hoping.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, here are my chance, I want to ask all three of you to do the dance with me.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No. No.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Come on.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I got in a little there, Maggie.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gio? Anyone? Anyone?\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Maggie, you're doing the Oompa-Loompa so well on TV.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm glad you're doing it, Maggie. Appreciate you.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We love you, Mags. What a gat interview and we will have more of the cast of "Wonka," including Timothee Chalamet and Keegan-Michael Key right here on "GMA" this week. And 'tis the season for gift wrapping hacks. Will Ganss weighs in on which ones will and won't work when we come back.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Will and Archie.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bv\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POLITICAL HEADLINES ON THE DEBATE STAGE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,257 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And welcome back here to "GMA." It was a big week of political headlines, so you know we have to take a closer look here. Here to break it all down, ABC's White House correspondent MaryAlice Parks in Iowa this morning, and our deputy political director Averi Harper here in our studio. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE YOUR VOTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON THE DEBATE STAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP CANDIDATES LOOK TO STAND OUT\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. Averi, let's start with you, because we saw that GOP debate. It was intense. It got heated. But we're getting closer and closer to that first primary. Did this debate change anything?\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I do not think it changed the trajectory of this race much at all. When we look at what happened on the debate stage, what we really saw were candidates who were willing to criticize one another, attack one another. But the main challenge for each and every one of those candidates is former President Trump. He is still far how, out ahead of each of every one of these candidates when you look at recent polling, and there is a real reluctance within this GOP field, with the exception of Christie, to criticize former President Trump. And that's because it's not popular within the Republican Party to criticize him. And so, we're gonna see what happens as some of those voters start to head to the polls in just about a month.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And let's, MaryAlice, let's bring you into the conversation here because you pressed the White House over, this week over President Biden's comments, implying that maybe he wouldn't have run for a second term if Trump were not in the race. How do they plan to take that message to the voters now?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WAS BIDEN AFFECTED BY TRUMP'S ACTIONS?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IMPLIED THAT HE MAY HAVE NOT RUN IF TRUMP DID NOT ENTER RACE\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, they really tried to down play this. They tried to say it was not a news story, that they, that the President was not implying that Trump was the only reason that he was running. But, of course, that's what everyone was reacting to because it did sound like if Trump wasn't on the ballot, he maybe wouldn't be as excited, as up for running. So, what happens if Trump is not the nominee, if he's not passionate about running if he has to face someone else? Even at his age, is he up for the task?\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, we've seen a lot of polls that have implied to us that Democrats might be more interested in supporting another Democrat besides President Biden. So, I also asked the White House about whether the President really thought that he was the only person that could be beat former President Trump. You know, there's an argument to be made that if they are so worried about the potential threat of a second Trump presidency, should they be looking at another candidate who might actually do better against former President Trump? You can imagine, Whit, they also totally brushed off that question.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP TALKS ABOUT BEING A ONE-DAY DICTATOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AGENDA ON POTENTIAL FIRST DAY IN OFFICE MAKING HEADLINES\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And speaking of President Trump, he made some waves with a comment he made recently talking about how he would only be a dictator on day one, Averi. Some Republicans have brushed it off as a joke and saying not to take it literally, others, like \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , saying we should take everything he says literally. What do you make of it, and how do voters respond to this?\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. It's definitely stoking some concerns. When we looked at that town hall on Fox News, the former president said that not only would he describe what he would do on day one as a dictator, he used the word dictator, but he also said that he would not rule out abusing the power of the presidency amid a second term if he were to be reelected. And so, yes, we heard some folks, we asked \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  after the debate earlier this week, he said he thought it was a joke.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But there are others, like \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  who sat down with ABC's \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2 , who says that we should take those comments seriously and we should take those comments literally. The Biden campaign also seized on those comments. So, it's definitely stoking concerns about what a second Trump presidency could look like.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AFFORDABLE CARE ACT IN THE BULLSEYE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICANS LOOKING FOR ALTERNATIVES\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. And MaryAlice, let's turn to a topic that's on so many minds, health care. Republicans are, are talking about repealing the Affordable Care Act. The Biden team, though, seems to be leaning into that.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. They really jumped on those comments, Gio, from Republicans about potentially trying to repeal and replace Obamacare if elected. Health care is absolutely the kind of issues that voters are talking about. They're concerned about hospital bills. They're concerned about the costs, the lack of availability of elder care, long-term care. You know, it's interesting, Obamacare actually, though, is really increasingly popular. Enrollment numbers are up from last year.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's open enrollment season right now. The numbers are strong again. You know, we're in western Iowa, really close to South Dakota and as evidence of just how popular that, the law is, this summer South Dakota voters demanded that South Dakota expand access to Medicaid, as they can do under the law. It was the seventh state that actually passed a ballot measure to go around their Republican governor to expand the law in the state. So, Democrats definitely see an opening here in defending the Affordable Care Act, guys.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, MaryAlice Parks for us in Iowa. It's definitely December there. We can see you all bundled, bundled up. Averi Harper here in the studio. It's great to have you both on this morning. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: CRIME RING TARGETS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Still ahead here on "Good Morning America," the suspected crime rings targeting high-end neighborhoods across the country, and why having an alarm system may not be good enough.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bi\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEALS & STEALS GIFTS GALORE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,424 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 