NG AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 INFANT MORTALITY, HEALTH CARE, DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 HANUKKAH, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PILO, KEIDAR\par \par \uc2 PRICE, NYBERG, GARCIA, QUIMBY, ESCOBAR, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE PEOPLE FEEDING THE PEOPLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW THE HOUSTON FOOD BANK PROVIDES "FOOD FOR BETTER LIVES"\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, let's go back to Somara for another check of the weather. Hey, Somara.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hi. Oh, my heart is so warm. Thank you for that. All right, so we're headed to Denver, Colorado, where they are waking up in their winter wonderland. One to two inches fell there, but up to ten inches in the mountain.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMY WEATHER\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're tracking multiple storms. I want to talk about the one in the southeast prompting wind alerts, flood watches and even severe weather.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE THREAT\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If you live in the Tennessee Valley, down to New Orleans, up into Jacksonville, Huntsville, Alabama, the threat for severe weather looms through this evening. Large hail, damaging winds, and we could even see a few tornadoes spark up.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRACKING THE STORM\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That severe threat then makes its way into the southeast. Atlanta gear up for some storms early tomorrow morning. And finally, heavy rain along the I-95 corridor with snow further inland. That's a look at your forecast, let's see what's going on a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bs\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 COVID-19 HOSPITALIZATIONS ON THE RISE 15 STATES EXPERIENCING 'HIGH OR 'VERY HIGH' LEVELS OF RESPIRATORY ILLNESS ACTIVITY\b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just too much heartache for too many families out there. Jaclyn, thank you. And we turn to the rise in COVID-19 hospitalizations. With RSV and flu cases also ticking up, it comes as holiday gatherings get into full swing. ABC's Reena Roy is here now with more. Good morning, Reena.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVID-19 HOSPITALIZATIONS ON THE RISE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CDC: 15 STATES EXPERIENCING 'HIGH' OR 'VERY HIGH' LEVELS OF RESPIRATORY ILLNESS ACTIVITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONWIDE RESPIRATORY ILLNESS ACTIVITY\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Erielle, good morning to you. Yeah, it is that time of year again, right, a season when we're all celebrating but also dealing with all kinds of illnesses. We usually hear the numbers go up in the fall and winter because of travel and holiday gatherings, and this year it is no different. The CDC says 15 states plus New York City are experiencing high or very high levels of respiratory illness activity. And that means doctors are seeing more and more people coming in with things like fevers and a cough or a sore throat, usually from COVID, the common colds or the flu. RSV is also on the rise and about half of states are seeing an increase in flu and COVID cases.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) COVID hospitalizations have reached levels not seen since February, particularly among babies, young children, and older adults. However, they are lower than rates seen at the same time last year. Meanwhile, health officials are also tracking a rising COVID subvariant called JN.1 that's estimated to make up more than 20 percent of cases right now around the country. At this time, there is no evidence that JN.1 is more severe than previous variants.\par \par \uc2 REENA ROY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tests, vaccines and treatments are still expected to be effective, and health officials say getting your shots is the best thing you can do. And it's not too late. Now is actually a great time because it often takes up to two weeks to reach full protection after a dose and that is just in time for Christmas. Gio?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bb\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MATERNAL HEALTH CARE DISPARITY NEW REPORT: BABIES OF BLACK MOTHERS STILL SUFFER DEATH AT TWICE THE RATE OF OTHERS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,005 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL, WAR, CEASE-FIRE, WOODS, SKAU\par \par \uc2 TREATMENT, SICKLE CELL DISEASE, GENE EDITING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKTHROUGH GENE EDITING THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FDA\uc2  APPROVES NEW TREATMENTS FOR SICKLE CELL DISEASE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, COX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY HALTS WOMAN'S EMERGENCY PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 INFANT MORTALITY, HEALTH CARE, DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) All right, time now for our "GMA" cover story and the new CDC report revealing fetal and early infant deaths in the United States from 2020 to 2021 were still almost twice as high in babies born to black women compared to those born in white and Hispanic women.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MATERNAL HEALTH CARE DISPARITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW REPORT: BABIES OF BLACK MOTHERS STILL SUFFER DEATH AT TWICE THE RATE OF OTHERS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ABC News medical correspondent Dr. Darien Sutton is here to break it all down for us. Dr. Sutton, good morning to you. It's great to have you.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know you've been covering this and looking at this for a while. Why does this disparity still exist?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, Whit, it's concerning but it shouldn't be surprising. What we've seen prior in the studies and the results in terms of infant mortality and, in this case, perinatal mortality, which Is when you have an infant or fetal deaths weeks before delivery or weeks after delivery. Among black women, it remains high. The reasons why these numbers haven't changed mainly is because our health care systems and structures have not responded to these concerning numbers. And as far as the reasons overall why you can see this, are a variety of reasons. Number one, access. We're seeing an increased rate of maternity care deserts. That's quantified or qualified as a county that doesn't have access to an OB or an obstetrician.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) One-third of our counties in this country do not have access to an OB or an obstetrician. And many people believe that that's mainly rural. And while that's partly correct, 60% of maternity care deserts are rural, 40% are in the inner city. Also, in terms of health care coverage, we have approximately 8 million women in this country of reproductive age that do not have health care insurance. And that translates to no access to primary care, increased rates of untreated high blood pressure, diabetes, which create poor outcomes in terms of health.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And then, overall, when you look at black women who have health access, who have health care overage and high levels of education they still have disproportionately higher rates of poor outcomes compared to their white counterparts. And that reason behind that is discrimination, bias and racism, that translates as black women not being heard in terms of expressing concerns during their pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just unbelievable. Well, what's it going to take to see a difference here?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think, personally, there are a variety of things that we can do today to change this. Number one, in our policy in terms of access. Fixing these maternity care deserts by funding and expanding midwife care, that is one of the ways that we can help provide access to those in need. Expanding Medicaid. In states that have expanded Medicaid, we see improved outcomes among black women. Also, education of health care systems, health care providers in terms of the harmful effects of bias and discrimination. And then also, requiring hospitals to be transparent about the results, so that patients can make decisions. And then also, we can hold hospitals accountable to who's doing bad and how we can correct that.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is there something specific or are there symptom specific that women and their partners can be looking out for? And how can they be their own health advocate because we hear that so often?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think it's so important. Number one, I think it's always important to bring an advocate with you. I think its really important, when I walk into a room and I'm talking to a patient, I find comfort when there's someone else there because often, when you're sitting in that patient garb and that gown, it's difficult to hear what you need to hear, but also making sure that you understand the symptoms, the bleeding, pain, headaches, swelling of your hands and your face. These are all concerning symptoms during pregnancy that should be addressed.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Need to know when it doesn't feel normal it probably isn't.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Dr. Sutton, thank you as always for shedding your insights. We appreciate you.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Of course.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020231229ejc9000bp\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 09:00 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 488 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY BLOCKS EMERGENCY ABORTION\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, BAN, COX, SCOTUS, EXCEPTIONS, DUANE, STONE\par \par \uc2 TRACKING, STORM, FLOOD, WATCH\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, GAZA, CEASE-FIRE, HOSTAGES, WOOD, SKAU, BLINKEN, BARUCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAVY RAIN EXPECTED FROM DELAWARE TO MAINE\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, LIFE, MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, SHOOTING, MYRE, VICTIMS, STATEMENTS\par \par \uc2 UNLV, SHOOTING, POLITO, 911, CALLERS, GARCIA, DRUM, TAKEMARU, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RSV, FLU, JN.1, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 O'NEAL, "LOVE STORY", "PAPER MOON", FILMS, LIFE, LEGACY, FAWCETT\par \par \uc2 FLOOD, WATCH, FORECAST, RAINFALL, SNOWFALL\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FINALS, TOURNAMENT, LAS VEGAS, \uc2 PACERS\uc2 , LAKERS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VOTERS, TRUMP, 2024, DEBATE, BARRANCO, RICHMAN, UGWUEKE, DONOHUE, DOYLE, LEAR\par \par \uc2 FORECAST, STORM, RAIN, SNOW, COLE\par \par \uc2 GOP, DEBATE, BIDEN, TRUMP, DICTATOR, OBAMACARE\par \par \uc2 CRIME, TOURISM, BURGLARY, BOUCHARD\par \par \uc2 PAISLEY, SANTA, STORE, CHRISTMAS, GIFTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's our second hour.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS SUPREME COURT BLOCKS ABORTION RULING\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Breaking overnight, abortion battle. The Texas Supreme Court temporarily blocking a ruling that would have allowed a pregnant woman to get an emergency abortion.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK MATERNAL CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW REPORT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Perinatal death rates twice as high among babies of black mothers, compared to their white and Hispanic counterparts. Dr. Sutton is here to break down the new report. What he says has to change and what you need to know to keep yourself safe.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SERVING UP KINDNESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIGHTING HUNGER FOR THE HOLIDAYS\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And serving up kindness. The incredible organization and volunteers working overtime this holiday season to make sure no one goes hungry.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIGHTING LIGHT IN THE DARK TIMES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING HANUKKAH\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And tonight's the third night of Hanukkah, the eight-day-long festival of light. People around the world observing the holiday and finding the light in dark times.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE CAST OF "WONKA"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOLDEN TICKET\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And "GMA" getting the golden ticket.\par \par \uc2 MO